        "Then Isaac said to Jacob, “Please come close so I can touch you, my son, and know whether you are really my son Esau or not.”",
        "So Jacob came close to his father Isaac. Isaac touched him and said, “The voice is Jacob’s voice, but the hands are Esau’s hands.”",
        "He did not recognize him, because his hands were hairy like his brother Esau’s hands. So he blessed him.",
        "He asked, “Are you really my son Esau?” Jacob answered, “I am.”",
        "Isaac said, “Bring the food close to me, and I will eat some of my son’s wild game, so that I may bless you with all my heart.” Jacob brought it to him, and he ate. Then Jacob brought him wine, and he drank.",
        "Then his father Isaac said to him, “Come close now and kiss me, my son.”",
        "So he came close and kissed him. Isaac smelled his clothes and blessed him. He said, “See, my son smells like a field that the Lord has blessed.”",
        "“May God give you the dew from heaven and the rich soil of the earth, with plenty of grain and wine.”",
        "“May peoples serve you and nations bow down to you. Be master over your brothers, and may your mother’s sons bow down to you. May everyone who curses you be cursed, and may everyone who blesses you be blessed.”",
        "Isaac had just finished blessing Jacob, and Jacob had barely left his father Isaac, when his brother Esau came in from hunting.",
        "Esau also made a tasty meal and brought it to his father. He said to him, “Father, please sit up and eat some of your son’s wild game, so that you may bless me with all your heart.”",
        "His father Isaac asked him, “Who are you?” He answered, “I am your son, your firstborn, Esau.”",
        "Isaac began to shake very hard. He said, “Then who was it that hunted wild game and brought it to me? I ate all of it before you came, and I blessed him. And yes, he will be blessed!”",
        "When Esau heard his father’s words, he let out a loud and very bitter cry. He said to his father, “Bless me, me too, my father!”",
        "Isaac said, “Your brother came with trickery and took away your blessing.”",
        "Esau said, “Isn’t he rightly named Jacob (a name that means ‘he grabs the heel’)? He has tricked me and taken my place two times now. He took my birthright, and now he has taken my blessing.” Then he asked, “Haven’t you saved a blessing for me?”",
        "Isaac answered Esau, “Look, I have made him your master. I have given him all his relatives as servants, and I have provided him with grain and wine. So what can I do for you now, my son?”",
        "Esau said to his father, “Do you have only one blessing, my father? Bless me, me too, my father!” Then Esau cried out loud and wept.",
        "His father Isaac answered him, “Your home will be in the rich places of the earth, with the dew from heaven above.”",
        "“You will live by your sword, and you will serve your brother. But when you gain power, you will break his yoke off your neck.”",
        "Esau hated Jacob because of the blessing his father had given him. Esau said to himself, “The days of mourning for my father are coming soon. Then I will kill my brother Jacob.”",
        "Someone told Rebekah what her older son Esau had said. So she sent for her younger son Jacob and said to him, “Listen, your brother Esau is comforting himself with a plan to kill you.”",
        "“So now, my son, listen to me. Get up and run away to my brother Laban in Haran.”",
        "“Stay with him for a little while, until your brother’s rage cools down.”",
        "“When your brother’s anger turns away from you and he forgets what you did to him, I will send for you and bring you back from there. Why should I lose both of you in one day?”",
        "Then Rebekah said to Isaac, “I am sick of my life because of these daughters of Heth (Hittite women). If Jacob marries one of the daughters of Heth like these, one of the women of this land, what good will my life be to me?”"
