        "These kings went to war against Bera king of Sodom, Birsha king of Gomorrah, Shinab king of Admah, Shemeber king of Zeboiim, and the king of Bela (also called Zoar).",
        "The five kings all joined forces in the valley of Siddim, which is now the Salt Sea (the Dead Sea).",
        "For twelve years they had been under Chedorlaomer’s rule, but in the thirteenth year they rose up against him.",
        "In the fourteenth year Chedorlaomer and the kings on his side came and defeated the Rephaims in Ashteroth Karnaim, the Zuzims in Ham, and the Emims in Shaveh Kiriathaim,",
        "and the Horites in their hill country of Seir, as far as El-paran, which is next to the wilderness.",
        "Then they turned back and came to En-mishpat, also called Kadesh. They conquered the whole land of the Amalekites, and also the Amorites who lived in Hazezon-tamar.",
        "Then the king of Sodom, the king of Gomorrah, the king of Admah, the king of Zeboiim, and the king of Bela (also called Zoar) marched out. They lined up for battle against the other kings in the valley of Siddim,",
        "against Chedorlaomer king of Elam, Tidal king of nations, Amraphel king of Shinar, and Arioch king of Ellasar. It was four kings against five.",
        "The valley of Siddim was full of tar pits. When the kings of Sodom and Gomorrah ran away, they fell into them, and the rest escaped to the hills.",
        "The winning kings took all the goods and all the food of Sodom and Gomorrah, and went on their way.",
        "They also took Lot, the son of Abram’s brother, who was living in Sodom. They took him and everything he owned, and left.",
        "A man who got away came and told Abram the Hebrew. Abram was living by the oak trees of Mamre the Amorite, the brother of Eshcol and Aner. These men had made a pact with Abram.",
        "When Abram heard that his relative had been captured, he called out his 318 trained men, who had been born in his household. They chased the enemy as far as Dan.",
        "At night Abram split his men into groups and attacked. He and his servants defeated the enemy and chased them as far as Hobah, north of Damascus.",
        "He brought back all the goods. He also brought back his relative Lot and Lot’s goods, along with the women and the other people.",
        "After Abram came back from defeating Chedorlaomer and the kings with him, the king of Sodom went out to meet him in the valley of Shaveh, which is the King’s Valley.",
        "Then Melchizedek king of Salem brought out bread and wine. He was the priest of the Most High God.",
        "He blessed Abram and said, “May Abram be blessed by the Most High God, who owns heaven and earth.”",
        "“And blessed be the Most High God, who has handed your enemies over to you.” Then Abram gave him a tenth of everything.",
        "The king of Sodom said to Abram, “Give me the people, and keep the goods for yourself.”",
        "But Abram said to the king of Sodom, “I have raised my hand in an oath to the Lord, the Most High God, who owns heaven and earth.”",
        "“I promised that I will not take anything of yours, not even a thread or a sandal strap. Then you can never say, ‘I made Abram rich.’”",
        "“I will take nothing except what my young men have already eaten. But let the men who went with me, Aner, Eshcol, and Mamre, take their share.”"
