      "ch": "Genesis 32",
      "verses": [
        "Jacob went on his way, and angels of God came to meet him.",
        "When Jacob saw them, he said, “This is God’s camp.” So he named that place Mahanaim (which means “two camps”).",
        "Jacob sent messengers ahead of him to his brother Esau, to the land of Seir, the country of Edom.",
        "He told them, “Say this to my lord Esau: ‘Your servant Jacob says this: I have been living as a stranger with Laban, and I stayed there until now.’”",
        "“I have cattle and donkeys, flocks, and male and female servants. I have sent this message to tell my lord, hoping you will be kind to me.”",
        "The messengers came back to Jacob and said, “We went to your brother Esau. He is coming to meet you, and four hundred men are with him.”",
        "Jacob was very afraid and upset. So he split the people who were with him, and the flocks, the herds, and the camels, into two groups.",
        "He thought, “If Esau comes to one group and attacks it, the group that is left can get away.”",
        "Then Jacob prayed, “O God of my father Abraham and God of my father Isaac, O Lord, You told me, ‘Go back to your country and to your family, and I will treat you well.’”",
        "“I don’t deserve the smallest part of all the kindness and faithfulness You have shown me, Your servant. When I crossed this Jordan River, all I had was my walking stick. Now I have become two camps.”",
        "“Please save me from my brother Esau. I am afraid of him. I am afraid he will come and attack me, and the mothers along with the children.”",
        "“But You said, ‘I will surely be good to you, and I will make your descendants like the sand of the sea, too many to count.’”",
        "Jacob spent the night there. From what he had with him, he chose a gift for his brother Esau:",
        "two hundred female goats and twenty male goats, two hundred female sheep and twenty rams,",
        "thirty camels that were nursing their young, forty cows and ten bulls, and twenty female donkeys and ten young male donkeys.",
        "He put each herd in the care of a servant, every herd by itself. He told his servants, “Go on ahead of me, and leave space between one herd and the next.”",
        "He told the man in front, “When my brother Esau meets you and asks, ‘Who do you belong to? Where are you going? Who owns these animals in front of you?’”",
        "“Then say, ‘They belong to your servant Jacob. They are a gift sent to my lord Esau. And look, Jacob himself is coming behind us.’”",
        "He gave the same orders to the second servant, the third, and all who followed the herds: “Say the same thing to Esau when you meet him.”",
        "“And be sure to say, ‘Your servant Jacob is right behind us.’” For Jacob thought, “I will calm his anger with the gift that goes ahead of me. After that I will face him. Maybe he will welcome me.”",
        "So the gift went on ahead of him, but Jacob himself spent that night in the camp.",
        "That night Jacob got up. He took his two wives, his two female servants, and his eleven sons, and crossed the shallow place in the Jabbok River.",
        "He took them and sent them across the stream, and he sent across everything he owned.",
        "Then Jacob was left alone, and a man wrestled with him until dawn.",
        "When the man saw that he could not win against Jacob, he touched the socket of Jacob’s hip, and Jacob’s hip was pulled out of joint as they wrestled.",
        "The man said, “Let me go, because the sun is coming up.” But Jacob said, “I won’t let you go unless you bless me.”",
        "The man asked him, “What is your name?” He answered, “Jacob.”",
        "Then the man said, “Your name will not be Jacob anymore, but Israel, because you have struggled with God and with men, and you have won.”",
        "Jacob asked him, “Please tell me your name.” But he said, “Why do you ask my name?” And he blessed Jacob there.",
        "So Jacob named the place Peniel (which means “the face of God”), because he said, “I have seen God face to face, and my life was spared.”",
        "The sun rose on him as he passed Penuel, and he was limping because of his hip.",
        "That is why, to this day, the children of Israel do not eat the tendon that shrank, which is on the hip socket. It is because the man touched the socket of Jacob’s hip at that tendon."
      ],
