        "Joseph went and told Pharaoh, “My father and my brothers have come from the land of Canaan with their flocks, their herds, and everything they own. They are now in the land of Goshen.”",
        "He chose five of his brothers and introduced them to Pharaoh.",
        "Pharaoh asked his brothers, “What work do you do?” They answered Pharaoh, “Your servants are shepherds, just as our fathers were.”",
        "They also said to Pharaoh, “We have come to live in the land for a while, because there is no pasture for your servants’ flocks. The famine is very bad in the land of Canaan. So please let your servants live in the land of Goshen.”",
        "Pharaoh said to Joseph, “Your father and your brothers have come to you.”",
        "“The land of Egypt is open to you. Settle your father and brothers in the best part of the land; let them live in the land of Goshen. And if you know of any capable men among them, put them in charge of my own livestock.”",
        "Then Joseph brought in his father Jacob and had him stand before Pharaoh, and Jacob blessed Pharaoh.",
        "Pharaoh asked Jacob, “How old are you?”",
        "Jacob answered Pharaoh, “I have been traveling through life for a hundred and thirty years. My years have been few and hard, and they have not reached the years my fathers lived in their travels.”",
        "Then Jacob blessed Pharaoh and left his presence.",
        "So Joseph settled his father and brothers and gave them property in the land of Egypt, in the best part of the land, in the land of Rameses, as Pharaoh had ordered.",
        "Joseph provided food for his father, his brothers, and all his father’s household, giving each family food according to how many children it had.",
        "There was no food anywhere in the land, because the famine was very severe. The land of Egypt and the land of Canaan were worn out because of the famine.",
        "Joseph collected all the money that could be found in the land of Egypt and the land of Canaan in payment for the grain people were buying, and he brought the money into Pharaoh’s palace.",
        "When the money in the land of Egypt and the land of Canaan was used up, all the Egyptians came to Joseph and said, “Give us food! Why should we die right in front of you? Our money is all gone.”",
        "Joseph said, “Bring me your livestock. If your money is gone, I will give you food in exchange for your livestock.”",
        "So they brought their livestock to Joseph, and he gave them food in exchange for their horses, their flocks, their herds of cattle, and their donkeys. That year he kept them fed in exchange for all their livestock.",
        "When that year was over, they came to him the next year and said, “We can’t hide from my lord that our money is gone, and our herds of livestock now belong to my lord. Nothing is left for my lord except our bodies and our land.”",
        "“Why should we die before your eyes, both we and our land? Buy us and our land in exchange for food, and we and our land will be servants to Pharaoh. Give us seed so we can live and not die, and so the land won’t become empty and wasted.”",
        "So Joseph bought all the land of Egypt for Pharaoh. Every Egyptian sold his field, because the famine was so hard on them. So the land became Pharaoh’s.",
        "As for the people, he moved them into the cities, from one end of Egypt’s borders to the other.",
        "Only the priests’ land he did not buy. The priests received a fixed share of food from Pharaoh, and they lived on the share Pharaoh gave them. That is why they didn’t sell their land.",
        "Then Joseph said to the people, “Listen, today I have bought you and your land for Pharaoh. Here is seed for you. Plant it in the land.”",
        "“When the harvest comes, give a fifth of it to Pharaoh. The other four parts will be yours, to use as seed for the fields and as food for yourselves, your households, and your little children.”",
        "They said, “You have saved our lives! May we have my lord’s favor, and we will be Pharaoh’s servants.”",
        "So Joseph made it a law over the land of Egypt, still in force today, that a fifth of the harvest belongs to Pharaoh. Only the priests’ land did not become Pharaoh’s.",
        "So Israel lived in the land of Egypt, in the region of Goshen. They gained property there, had many children, and grew greatly in number.",
        "Jacob lived in the land of Egypt for seventeen years. In all, Jacob lived a hundred and forty-seven years.",
