        "If a man lets his animals graze in a field or vineyard, and lets them loose so they feed in another man’s field, he must pay it back from the best of his own field and the best of his own vineyard.",
        "If a fire starts and spreads into thornbushes, so that it burns up stacked grain, standing grain, or the whole field, the person who started the fire must pay for all of it.",
        "If a man gives his neighbor money or goods to keep safe, and they are stolen from that neighbor’s house, the thief must pay back double if he is caught.",
        "If the thief is not caught, the owner of the house must come before the judges, so they can find out whether he took his neighbor’s things himself.",
        "In every case of wrongdoing about an ox, a donkey, a sheep, clothing, or anything lost that someone claims is his, both sides must bring their case to the judges. The one the judges find guilty must pay his neighbor back double.",
        "If a man gives his neighbor a donkey, an ox, a sheep, or any other animal to take care of, and it dies, gets hurt, or is driven off while no one sees it,",
        "then the two of them must settle it by an oath before the Lord that he did not take his neighbor’s property. The owner must accept the oath, and the neighbor does not have to pay.",
