        "If it was torn apart by a wild animal, he must bring what is left as proof, and he does not have to pay for the torn animal.",
        "If a man borrows something from his neighbor, and it gets hurt or dies while its owner is not there, he must pay for it in full.",
        "But if the owner was there with it, he does not have to pay. If it was rented, the rent covers the loss.",
        "If a man talks a young woman who is not engaged into sleeping with him, he must pay the bride-price and make her his wife.",
        "If her father absolutely refuses to give her to him, he must still pay money equal to the bride-price for a young woman who has never married.",
        "You must not let a witch live.",
