        "He spoke to the congregation and said, “Please move away from the tents of these wicked men! Don’t touch anything that belongs to them, or you will be swept away in all their sins.”",
        "So the people moved away from all around the tents of Korah, Dathan, and Abiram. Dathan and Abiram came out and stood at the doors of their tents with their wives, their sons, and their little children.",
        "Then Moses said, “Here is how you will know that the Lord sent me to do all these things, and that it was not my own idea.”",
        "“If these men die a normal death like everyone else, or if what happens to all people happens to them, then the Lord has not sent me.”",
        "“But if the Lord does something new, and the ground opens its mouth and swallows them and everything they have, and they go down alive into the world of the dead, then you will understand that these men have treated the Lord with scorn.”",
        "As soon as he finished saying all these words, the ground under them split open.",
        "The earth opened its mouth and swallowed them, with their households, all of Korah’s men, and everything they owned.",
        "They and everything that belonged to them went down alive into the world of the dead. The earth closed over them, and they were gone from among the congregation.",
        "All the Israelites around them ran away when they heard them scream. They said, “The earth might swallow us up too!”",
        "Then fire came out from the Lord and burned up the 250 men who were offering incense.",
        "The Lord spoke to Moses. He said,",
        "“Tell Eleazar, the son of Aaron the priest, to take the censers out of the burning remains and scatter the coals far away, because the censers are holy.”",
        "“These men sinned, and it cost them their lives. Hammer their censers into flat sheets to cover the altar. They were offered before the Lord, so they are holy. They will be a sign to the people of Israel.”",
        "So Eleazar the priest took the bronze censers that had been offered by the men who were burned up, and they were hammered into flat sheets to cover the altar.",
        "They were a reminder to the people of Israel that no outsider who is not a descendant of Aaron should come near to burn incense before the Lord, so he would not become like Korah and his group. This was just as the Lord had told him through Moses.",
        "But the next day the whole congregation of the people of Israel complained against Moses and Aaron. They said, “You have killed the Lord’s people!”",
        "While the congregation was gathering against Moses and Aaron, they turned toward the tent of meeting, and suddenly the cloud covered it and the glory of the Lord appeared.",
        "Moses and Aaron went to the front of the tent of meeting.",
        "The Lord said to Moses,",
        "“Get away from this congregation, so I can destroy them in a moment.” And they fell on their faces.",
        "Moses said to Aaron, “Take a censer, put fire from the altar in it, and add incense. Hurry to the congregation and make an atonement for them, because anger has gone out from the Lord. The plague has started.”",
        "Aaron did as Moses said and ran into the middle of the congregation. The plague had already started among the people. He put on the incense and made an atonement for the people.",
        "He stood between the dead and the living, and the plague stopped.",
        "Those who died in the plague numbered 14,700, besides those who died because of what Korah did.",
        "Then Aaron went back to Moses at the door of the tent of meeting, because the plague had stopped."
