        "Balaam saw that the Lord was pleased to bless Israel. So he did not go looking for magic signs as he had the other times. Instead, he turned to face the wilderness.",
        "Balaam looked up and saw Israel camped tribe by tribe. Then the Spirit of God came upon him.",
        "He spoke his prophecy: “This is the message of Balaam the son of Beor, the message of the man whose eyes are open.”",
        "“This is the message of the one who hears God’s words and sees a vision from the Almighty, who falls down in a trance, but with his eyes open.”",
        "“How beautiful your tents are, Jacob, and your homes, Israel!”",
        "“They spread out like valleys, like gardens beside a river, like aloe trees the Lord has planted, like cedar trees beside the water.”",
        "“Water will pour from his buckets, and his seed will have plenty of water. His king will be greater than Agag, and his kingdom will be raised high.”",
        "“God brought him out of Egypt. He has strength like the horns of a wild ox. He will eat up the nations that are his enemies. He will break their bones and pierce them with his arrows.”",
        "“He crouches and lies down like a lion, like a great lion. Who would dare to wake him up? Blessed are those who bless you, and cursed are those who curse you.”",
        "Balak became very angry with Balaam. He struck his hands together and said to Balaam, “I called you here to curse my enemies, and look, you have blessed them three times!”",
        "“So now hurry back home! I said I would give you great honor, but look, the Lord has kept you from being honored.”",
        "Balaam answered Balak, “Didn’t I tell the messengers you sent me this very thing?”",
        "“I said, ‘Even if Balak gave me his house full of silver and gold, I could not go against the Lord’s command to do anything good or bad on my own. I will say only what the Lord says.’”",
        "“Now I am going back to my people. But come, I will tell you what these people will do to your people in the last days.”",
        "Then he spoke his prophecy: “This is the message of Balaam the son of Beor, the message of the man whose eyes are open.”",
        "“This is the message of the one who hears God’s words, who knows what the Most High knows, and who sees a vision from the Almighty, who falls down in a trance, but with his eyes open.”",
        "“I see him, but not now. I look at him, but he is not near. A Star will come out of Jacob, and a Scepter (a king’s staff) will rise out of Israel. He will crush the corners of Moab and destroy all the children of Sheth.”",
        "“Edom will be taken over. Seir also will be taken over by its enemies. But Israel will act with great courage.”",
        "“A ruler will come out of Jacob and destroy those who are left in the city.”",
        "Then Balaam looked at Amalek and spoke his prophecy: “Amalek was the first of the nations, but in the end he will be destroyed forever.”",
        "Then he looked at the Kenites and spoke his prophecy: “Your home is strong, and your nest is set in the rock.”",
        "“Even so, the Kenites will be wiped out, when Asshur (Assyria) carries you away as prisoners.”",
        "Then he spoke his prophecy again: “Oh no! Who can live when God does this?”",
        "“Ships will come from the coast of Chittim (Cyprus). They will crush Asshur and crush Eber, but he too will be destroyed forever.”",
        "Then Balaam got up and went back home, and Balak also went on his way."
