      "ch": "Numbers 13",
      "verses": [
        "The Lord spoke to Moses. He said,",
        "“Send men to explore the land of Canaan, which I am giving to the people of Israel. Send one man from each of their fathers’ tribes, each one a leader among them.”",
        "So at the Lord’s command, Moses sent them out from the wilderness of Paran. All of them were leaders of the people of Israel.",
        "These were their names: from the tribe of Reuben, Shammua son of Zaccur;",
        "from the tribe of Simeon, Shaphat son of Hori;",
        "from the tribe of Judah, Caleb son of Jephunneh;",
        "from the tribe of Issachar, Igal son of Joseph;",
        "from the tribe of Ephraim, Oshea son of Nun;",
        "from the tribe of Benjamin, Palti son of Raphu;",
        "from the tribe of Zebulun, Gaddiel son of Sodi;",
        "from the tribe of Joseph, that is, the tribe of Manasseh, Gaddi son of Susi;",
        "from the tribe of Dan, Ammiel son of Gemalli;",
        "from the tribe of Asher, Sethur son of Michael;",
        "from the tribe of Naphtali, Nahbi son of Vophsi;",
        "from the tribe of Gad, Geuel son of Machi.",
        "These are the names of the men Moses sent to explore the land. Moses gave Oshea son of Nun the name Jehoshua (Joshua).",
        "When Moses sent them to explore the land of Canaan, he told them, “Go up this way through the south country, the Negev, and go up into the hill country.”",
        "“See what the land is like. See whether the people living there are strong or weak, and whether there are few or many.”",
        "“See whether the land they live in is good or bad. See whether their towns are open camps or have strong walls.”",
        "“See whether the soil is rich or poor, and whether there are trees in it or not. Be brave, and bring back some of the fruit of the land.” It was the season when the first grapes were ripe.",
        "So they went up and explored the land from the wilderness of Zin as far as Rehob, near the road to Hamath.",
        "They went up through the south country and came to Hebron, where Ahiman, Sheshai, and Talmai lived. They were descendants of Anak. (Hebron had been built seven years before Zoan in Egypt.)",
        "They came to the valley of Eshcol. There they cut off a branch with a single cluster of grapes, and two of them carried it on a pole between them. They also brought some pomegranates and figs.",
        "That place was called the valley of Eshcol (cluster) because of the cluster of grapes the people of Israel cut there.",
        "After forty days they came back from exploring the land.",
        "They came back to Moses, Aaron, and the whole community of Israel in the wilderness of Paran, at Kadesh. They gave their report to them and to the whole community, and showed them the fruit of the land.",
        "This is what they told Moses: “We went into the land where you sent us, and it really does flow with milk and honey! Here is some of its fruit.”",
        "“But the people who live in the land are strong. The cities have walls and are very large. We even saw the descendants of Anak there.”",
        "“The Amalekites live in the south country. The Hittites, the Jebusites, and the Amorites live in the hill country. The Canaanites live by the sea and along the Jordan River.”",
        "Then Caleb quieted the people in front of Moses and said, “Let’s go up right now and take the land. We can surely conquer it!”",
        "But the men who had gone up with him said, “We can’t go up against those people. They are stronger than we are!”",
        "So they spread a bad report among the people of Israel about the land they had explored. They said, “The land we went through to explore is a land that eats up the people who live in it. All the people we saw there are very tall.”",
        "“There we saw the giants (the Nephilim), the sons of Anak, who come from the giants. In our own eyes we were like grasshoppers, and that is how we looked to them too.”"
      ],
