        "That night the whole community cried out loud, and the people wept.",
        "All the people of Israel complained against Moses and Aaron. The whole community said to them, “We wish we had died in the land of Egypt! Or we wish we had died in this wilderness!”",
        "“Why is the Lord bringing us into this land just to be killed by the sword? Our wives and children will be taken as plunder. Wouldn’t it be better for us to go back to Egypt?”",
        "And they said to each other, “Let’s choose a leader and go back to Egypt.”",
        "Then Moses and Aaron fell face down in front of the whole gathered community of Israel.",
        "Joshua son of Nun and Caleb son of Jephunneh, two of the men who had explored the land, tore their clothes.",
        "They said to the whole community of Israel, “The land we went through to explore is a very, very good land.”",
        "“If the Lord is pleased with us, He will bring us into this land and give it to us. It is a land flowing with milk and honey.”",
        "“Just don’t rebel against the Lord, and don’t be afraid of the people of the land. We will eat them up like bread. Their protection is gone, and the Lord is with us. Don’t be afraid of them!”",
        "But the whole community talked of stoning them to death. Then the glory of the Lord appeared at the tent of meeting to all the people of Israel.",
        "The Lord said to Moses, “How long will these people treat Me with contempt? How long will they refuse to believe Me, even after all the signs I have done among them?”",
        "“I will strike them with a deadly disease and take away their inheritance. Then I will make you into a nation greater and stronger than they are.”",
        "But Moses said to the Lord, “Then the Egyptians will hear about it! You used Your power to bring these people out from among them.”",
        "“They will tell the people who live in this land. They have already heard that You, Lord, are with these people. They know that You, Lord, are seen face to face, that Your cloud stands over them, and that You go ahead of them in a pillar of cloud by day and a pillar of fire by night.”",
        "“If You kill all these people at once, the nations who have heard about You will say,”",
        "‘The Lord wasn’t able to bring these people into the land He promised them with an oath, so He killed them in the wilderness.’",
        "“So now, please, let my Lord’s power be shown to be great, just as You said:”",
        "‘The Lord is slow to anger and full of mercy. He forgives sin and rebellion. But He will not let the guilty go unpunished. He punishes the children for the sin of their fathers, to the third and fourth generation.’",
        "“Please forgive the sin of these people, because Your mercy is so great, just as You have forgiven them all the way from Egypt until now.”",
        "The Lord said, “I have forgiven them, as you asked.”",
        "“But as surely as I live, the whole earth will be filled with the glory of the Lord.”",
        "“All these men have seen My glory and the miracles I did in Egypt and in the wilderness. Yet they have tested Me these ten times and have not listened to My voice.”",
        "“So they will never see the land I promised with an oath to their fathers. None of those who treated Me with contempt will see it.”",
        "“But My servant Caleb has a different spirit in him and has followed Me with his whole heart. I will bring him into the land he went into, and his descendants will own it.”",
        "“(The Amalekites and the Canaanites live in the valley.) Tomorrow turn around and head into the wilderness, along the road to the Red Sea.”",
        "The Lord spoke to Moses and Aaron. He said,",
        "“How long must I put up with this wicked community that keeps complaining against Me? I have heard the complaints the people of Israel keep making against Me.”",
        "“Tell them this: As surely as I live, says the Lord, I will do to you exactly what I heard you say.”",
        "“Your dead bodies will fall in this wilderness: all of you who were counted in the census, everyone twenty years old and older, who complained against Me.”",
        "“Not one of you will enter the land I swore to give you as your home, except Caleb son of Jephunneh and Joshua son of Nun.”",
        "“But your little ones, the ones you said would be taken as plunder, I will bring in. They will come to know the land you have rejected.”",
        "“But as for you, your dead bodies will fall in this wilderness.”",
        "“Your children will wander in the wilderness for forty years. They will suffer for your unfaithfulness until the last of your bodies lies dead in the wilderness.”",
        "“You explored the land for forty days. So for forty years, one year for each day, you will carry the guilt of your sins. Then you will know what it means to have Me turn against you.”",
        "“I, the Lord, have spoken. I will surely do these things to this whole wicked community that has gathered together against Me. They will come to their end in this wilderness, and there they will die.”",
        "Moses had sent men to explore the land. They came back and made the whole community complain against him by spreading a bad report about the land.",
        "Those men who spread the bad report about the land died of a plague before the Lord.",
        "But Joshua son of Nun and Caleb son of Jephunneh, who were among the men who went to explore the land, stayed alive.",
        "When Moses told all the people of Israel these words, the people mourned bitterly.",
        "Early the next morning they got up and went up toward the top of the mountain. They said, “Here we are! We will go up to the place the Lord promised, because we have sinned.”",
