        "Then the Israelites moved on and camped in the plains of Moab, beside the Jordan River, across from Jericho.",
        "Balak the son of Zippor saw everything Israel had done to the Amorites.",
        "Moab was terrified of the people, because there were so many of them. The Moabites were filled with dread because of the Israelites.",
        "Moab said to the leaders of Midian, “This crowd will now lick up everything around us, the way an ox licks up the grass in a field.” Balak the son of Zippor was king of Moab at that time.",
        "He sent messengers to call Balaam the son of Beor at Pethor, which is by the river (the Euphrates), in the land of his own people. Balak’s message said, “Look, a people has come out of Egypt. They cover the whole land, and they have settled right next to me.”",
        "“So please come now and put a curse on these people for me, because they are too strong for me. Maybe then I can defeat them and drive them out of the land. I know that the people you bless are blessed, and the people you curse are cursed.”",
        "The leaders of Moab and of Midian left, carrying the payment for fortune-telling. They came to Balaam and told him what Balak had said.",
        "Balaam told them, “Stay here tonight, and I will bring you back whatever answer the Lord gives me.” So the princes of Moab stayed with Balaam.",
        "Then God came to Balaam and said, “Who are these men here with you?”",
        "Balaam told God, “Balak the son of Zippor, king of Moab, has sent a message to me.”",
