        "They wore old, patched sandals and worn-out clothes, and all the bread they brought was dry and crumbling.",
        "They went to Joshua at the camp at Gilgal and said to him and the men of Israel, “We have come from a faraway country. So please make a treaty with us.”",
        "The men of Israel said to the Hivites, “Maybe you live among us. How can we make a treaty with you?”",
        "They said to Joshua, “We are your servants.” Joshua asked them, “Who are you, and where do you come from?”",
        "They answered, “Your servants have come from a very faraway country because of the name of the Lord your God. We have heard about Him and everything He did in Egypt,”",
        "“and everything He did to the two kings of the Amorites on the other side of the Jordan: Sihon king of Heshbon, and Og king of Bashan, who lived at Ashtaroth.”",
        "“So our elders and everyone who lives in our country told us to take food for the trip, go and meet you, and tell you that we are your servants and ask you to make a treaty with us.”",
        "“This bread of ours was still warm when we packed it at home the day we left to come to you. But look, now it is dry and crumbling.”",
        "“These wineskins were new when we filled them, but look, they are split open. And our clothes and sandals are worn out from our very long trip.”",
        "The Israelite men took some of their food, but they did not ask the Lord what to do.",
        "Joshua made peace with them and made a treaty to let them live. The leaders of the congregation swore an oath to them.",
        "Three days after they made the treaty, the Israelites heard that these people were their neighbors and lived among them.",
        "So the Israelites set out, and on the third day they came to their cities: Gibeon, Chephirah, Beeroth, and Kirjath-jearim.",
        "But the Israelites did not attack them, because the leaders of the congregation had sworn an oath to them in the name of the Lord God of Israel. And the whole congregation grumbled against the leaders.",
        "All the leaders answered the whole congregation, “We have sworn an oath to them by the Lord God of Israel, so we cannot touch them now.”",
