        "While the children of Israel were camped at Gilgal on the plains of Jericho, they kept the Passover on the evening of the fourteenth day of the month.",
        "The day after the Passover, on that very day, they ate some of the grain grown in the land: bread made without yeast, and roasted grain.",
        "The day after they ate food grown in the land, the manna stopped. The children of Israel never had manna again. That year they ate the crops of the land of Canaan.",
        "When Joshua was near Jericho, he looked up and saw a man standing in front of him holding a drawn sword. Joshua went up to Him and asked, “Are You on our side or on our enemies’ side?”",
        "“No,” He answered, “I have come now as the captain of the Lord’s army.” Joshua fell with his face to the ground and worshipped. He asked Him, “What does my Lord want to say to His servant?”",
        "The captain of the Lord’s army told Joshua, “Take your shoe off your foot, because the place where you are standing is holy.” And Joshua did it."
