        "His father-in-law, the young woman’s father, made him stay, and he stayed with him three days. They ate and drank and slept there.",
        "On the fourth day they got up early in the morning, and he got ready to leave. But the young woman’s father said to his son-in-law, “Have a bite of bread to give you strength, and then you can go.”",
        "So the two of them sat down and ate and drank together. Then the young woman’s father said to the man, “Please, stay the night and enjoy yourself.”",
        "When the man got up to leave, his father-in-law kept urging him, so he stayed there another night.",
        "On the fifth day he got up early in the morning to leave, but the young woman’s father said, “Please, eat something first to give you strength.” So they waited until afternoon, and the two of them ate together.",
        "When the man got up to leave with his concubine and his servant, his father-in-law, the young woman’s father, said to him, “Look, it is getting toward evening now. Please stay the night. The day is almost over. Stay here and enjoy yourself. Then tomorrow you can get up early and start your trip home.”",
        "But the man did not want to stay another night. He got up and left and came near Jebus, which is Jerusalem. He had his two saddled donkeys with him, and his concubine was with him too.",
        "When they were near Jebus, the day was almost gone. The servant said to his master, “Come on, please, let’s stop at this city of the Jebusites and spend the night in it.”",
        "His master said to him, “We will not stop in a city of foreigners who are not Israelites. We will go on to Gibeah.”",
        "He said to his servant, “Come on, let’s try to reach one of these places and spend the night in Gibeah or in Ramah.”",
        "So they kept going, and the sun went down as they came near Gibeah, which belongs to the tribe of Benjamin.",
        "They turned off the road to go in and spend the night in Gibeah. He went in and sat down in the city square, but no one took them into his house for the night.",
        "Then an old man came in from his work in the field that evening. He was also from the hill country of Ephraim and was living as a stranger in Gibeah. The men of that place were from the tribe of Benjamin.",
        "The old man looked up and saw the traveler in the city square. He asked, “Where are you going? Where are you coming from?”",
        "He answered, “We are traveling from Beth-lehem-judah to the far edge of the hill country of Ephraim. That is where I am from. I went to Beth-lehem-judah, and now I am going to the house of the Lord. But no one will take me into his house.”",
        "“We have straw and feed for our donkeys, and bread and wine for me, for your servant girl, and for the young man with us your servants. We don’t need anything.”",
        "The old man said, “Peace be with you. Let me take care of whatever you need. Just don’t spend the night in the square.”",
        "So he brought him into his house and fed the donkeys. They washed their feet and ate and drank.",
        "While they were enjoying themselves, the men of the city, certain sons of Belial (worthless men), surrounded the house and pounded on the door. They said to the old man who owned the house, “Bring out the man who came into your house, so that we may know him (sleep with him).”",
        "The man who owned the house went out to them and said, “No, my brothers, no! Please don’t do such an evil thing. This man has come into my house as my guest. Don’t do this shameful thing.”",
        "“Look, here is my daughter, a virgin, and his concubine. Let me bring them out now. Abuse them and do whatever you want with them. But don’t do such a disgraceful thing to this man.”",
        "But the men would not listen to him. So the man took hold of his concubine and pushed her outside to them. They knew her (forced themselves on her) and abused her all night until morning. As the sun was coming up, they let her go.",
        "At daybreak the woman came and fell down at the door of the man’s house where her husband was, and she lay there until it was light.",
        "In the morning her husband got up, opened the doors of the house, and went out to go on his way. There was his concubine, fallen down at the door of the house, with her hands on the doorstep.",
        "He said to her, “Get up. Let’s go.” But there was no answer. Then the man put her on a donkey and set out for home.",
        "When he got home, he took a knife, took hold of his concubine, and cut her body, bones and all, into twelve pieces. He sent the pieces all through the land of Israel.",
        "Everyone who saw it said, “Nothing like this has ever happened or been seen from the day the Israelites came up out of the land of Egypt until today. Think about it, talk it over, and say what we should do.”"
