        "Jephthah from Gilead was a mighty, brave warrior. He was the son of a prostitute, and his father was Gilead.",
        "Gilead’s wife also gave him sons. When these sons grew up, they drove Jephthah away. They told him, “You will get no share of our father’s property, because you are the son of another woman.”",
        "So Jephthah ran away from his brothers and lived in the land of Tob. Some worthless men gathered around him there and went out with him.",
        "Some time later, the Ammonites went to war against Israel.",
        "When the Ammonites attacked Israel, the elders of Gilead went to bring Jephthah back from the land of Tob.",
        "They said to Jephthah, “Come and be our commander, so we can fight the Ammonites.”",
        "Jephthah said to the elders of Gilead, “Didn’t you hate me and throw me out of my father’s house? So why have you come to me now, when you are in trouble?”",
        "The elders of Gilead said to Jephthah, “That is exactly why we have come back to you now. Come with us, fight the Ammonites, and be our leader over everyone who lives in Gilead.”",
        "Jephthah said to the elders of Gilead, “If you bring me back home to fight the Ammonites, and the Lord hands them over to me, will I really be your leader?”",
        "The elders of Gilead said to Jephthah, “The Lord is listening and will be the witness between us. We will surely do what you say.”",
        "So Jephthah went with the elders of Gilead, and the people made him their leader and commander. And at Mizpeh Jephthah spoke all his words before the Lord.",
        "Then Jephthah sent messengers to the king of the Ammonites to ask, “What do you have against me, that you have come to attack my land?”",
        "The king of the Ammonites answered Jephthah’s messengers, “When Israel came up out of Egypt, they took my land, from the Arnon River to the Jabbok River and over to the Jordan. So now give those lands back peacefully.”",
        "Jephthah sent messengers again to the king of the Ammonites.",
        "They told him, “This is what Jephthah says: Israel did not take the land of Moab or the land of the Ammonites.”",
        "When Israel came up from Egypt, they traveled through the wilderness to the Red Sea and came to Kadesh.",
        "Then Israel sent messengers to the king of Edom to say, “Please let us pass through your land.” But the king of Edom would not listen. They sent the same request to the king of Moab, but he refused too. So Israel stayed at Kadesh.",
        "Then they traveled through the wilderness and went around the land of Edom and the land of Moab. They came along the east side of Moab and camped on the other side of the Arnon. They did not go inside Moab’s border, because the Arnon was the border of Moab.",
        "Then Israel sent messengers to Sihon king of the Amorites, who ruled from Heshbon. Israel said to him, “Please let us pass through your land to our own place.”",
        "But Sihon did not trust Israel to pass through his land. Instead, Sihon gathered all his army, camped at Jahaz, and fought against Israel.",
        "The Lord God of Israel handed Sihon and all his people over to Israel, and Israel defeated them. So Israel took over all the land of the Amorites who lived in that country.",
        "They took over all the land of the Amorites, from the Arnon to the Jabbok, and from the wilderness to the Jordan.",
        "So the Lord God of Israel has driven out the Amorites to make room for His people Israel. Should you now take it from us?",
        "Don’t you keep whatever land your god Chemosh gives you? In the same way, we will keep all the land the Lord our God has cleared for us.",
        "Are you any better than Balak the son of Zippor, king of Moab? Did he ever quarrel with Israel or go to war against them?",
        "Israel has lived in Heshbon and its villages, in Aroer and its villages, and in all the cities along the Arnon for three hundred years. Why didn’t you take them back during all that time?",
        "I have not wronged you. You are the one doing wrong by making war on me. Let the Lord, the Judge, decide today between the children of Israel and the Ammonites.",
        "But the king of the Ammonites would not listen to the message Jephthah sent him.",
        "Then the Spirit of the Lord came on Jephthah. He went through Gilead and Manasseh, then through Mizpeh in Gilead, and from Mizpeh in Gilead he went on against the Ammonites.",
        "Jephthah made a promise to the Lord. He said, “If You will truly hand the Ammonites over to me,”",
        "“then whatever comes out the door of my house to meet me when I come home safely from fighting the Ammonites will belong to the Lord. I will offer it up as a burnt offering.”",
        "So Jephthah went over to fight the Ammonites, and the Lord handed them over to him.",
        "He struck them down from Aroer to the area of Minnith, twenty cities, and as far as the plain of the vineyards. It was a huge defeat. So the Ammonites were brought under the control of the children of Israel.",
        "When Jephthah came home to Mizpeh, there was his daughter, coming out to meet him with tambourines and dancing! She was his only child. He had no other son or daughter.",
        "When he saw her, he tore his clothes and said, “Oh no, my daughter! You have crushed me! You have brought me terrible pain. I have made a promise to the Lord, and I cannot take it back.”",
        "She said to him, “My father, you have made a promise to the Lord. Do to me what you promised, since the Lord has paid back your enemies, the Ammonites, for you.”",
        "Then she said to her father, “Let me have this one thing. Give me two months to go and wander on the mountains with my friends and weep because I am still a virgin.”",
