        "Samson went to Gaza. He saw a prostitute there and went in to her.",
        "The people of Gaza were told, “Samson has come here.” So they surrounded the place and hid and waited for him all night at the city gate. They kept quiet all night, saying, “When morning comes and it is light, we will kill him.”",
        "But Samson lay there only until midnight. At midnight he got up, grabbed the doors of the city gate and the two gateposts, and pulled them up, crossbar and all. He put them on his shoulders and carried them up to the top of the hill that faces Hebron.",
