        "The rulers of the Philistines came to her and said, “Trick him into telling you what makes his strength so great, and how we can overpower him, so we can tie him up and bring him down. Each one of us will give you eleven hundred pieces of silver.”",
        "So Delilah said to Samson, “Please tell me what makes your strength so great, and what you could be tied up with to bring you down.”",
        "Samson told her, “If they tie me up with seven fresh cords that have never been dried, I will be weak, just like any other man.”",
        "So the rulers of the Philistines brought her seven fresh cords that had not been dried, and she tied him up with them.",
        "Men were hiding in her room, waiting to attack. She called to him, “Samson, the Philistines are coming at you!” But he snapped the cords as easily as a piece of string snaps when it touches fire. So the secret of his strength was still not known.",
        "Then Delilah said to Samson, “Look, you have made a fool of me and told me lies. Now please tell me what you could be tied up with.”",
        "He told her, “If they tie me up tight with new ropes that have never been used, I will be weak, just like any other man.”",
        "So Delilah took new ropes and tied him up with them. Then she called to him, “Samson, the Philistines are coming at you!” Men were hiding in the room, waiting. But he snapped the ropes off his arms as if they were thread.",
        "Then Delilah said to Samson, “Until now you have made a fool of me and told me lies. Tell me what you could be tied up with.” He told her, “If you weave the seven braids of my hair into the cloth on your loom.”",
        "So she fastened it tight with the pin and called to him, “Samson, the Philistines are coming at you!” He woke up from his sleep and pulled away the pin of the loom and the cloth with it.",
        "Then she said to him, “How can you say, ‘I love you,’ when your heart is not with me? Three times now you have made a fool of me, and you still have not told me what makes your strength so great.”",
        "She kept pushing him with her words day after day and begging him, until he was so worn out he wanted to die.",
        "So he told her everything in his heart. He said to her, “A razor has never touched my head, because I have been a Nazarite (someone set apart) to God from my mother’s womb. If my head is shaved, my strength will leave me. I will become weak, just like any other man.”",
        "When Delilah saw that he had told her everything in his heart, she sent for the rulers of the Philistines with this message: “Come up one more time, because he has told me everything in his heart.” So the rulers of the Philistines came up to her, bringing the money with them.",
        "She got him to fall asleep on her lap. Then she called a man and had him shave off the seven braids of Samson’s hair. She began to overpower him, and his strength left him.",
        "Then she said, “Samson, the Philistines are coming at you!” He woke up from his sleep and said, “I will go out as I did the other times and shake myself free.” But he did not know that the Lord had left him.",
        "The Philistines grabbed him and put out his eyes. They took him down to Gaza and tied him up with bronze chains, and he was made to grind grain in the prison.",
        "But after his head was shaved, his hair began to grow back.",
        "The rulers of the Philistines gathered together to offer a great sacrifice to their god Dagon and to celebrate. They said, “Our god has handed Samson our enemy over to us.”",
        "When the people saw him, they praised their god. They said, “Our god has handed our enemy over to us, the one who ruined our land and killed so many of us.”",
        "While they were in high spirits, they said, “Call for Samson so he can entertain us.” So they brought Samson out of the prison, and he entertained them. They made him stand between the pillars.",
        "Samson said to the young man who was leading him by the hand, “Let me feel the pillars that hold up the building, so I can lean against them.”",
        "The building was full of men and women. All the rulers of the Philistines were there, and on the roof were about three thousand men and women watching Samson entertain them.",
        "Then Samson called out to the Lord, “Lord God, please remember me. Please make me strong just this one more time, O God, so I can pay the Philistines back with one blow for my two eyes.”",
        "Samson took hold of the two middle pillars that held up the building, one with his right hand and the other with his left, and leaned his weight on them.",
