        "Early in the morning Jerubbaal (that is, Gideon) and all the men with him got up and camped beside the spring of Harod. The Midianite army was camped north of them, by the hill of Moreh, in the valley.",
        "The Lord said to Gideon, “You have too many men with you for Me to hand the Midianites over to them. Israel might brag against Me and say, ‘My own power saved me.’”",
        "“So now announce to the men, ‘Anyone who is scared and trembling may turn back and leave Mount Gilead.’” Twenty-two thousand men went home, and ten thousand stayed.",
        "But the Lord said to Gideon, “There are still too many men. Take them down to the water, and I will sort them out for you there. If I tell you, ‘This one will go with you,’ he will go. But if I tell you, ‘This one will not go with you,’ he will not go.”",
        "So Gideon took the men down to the water. The Lord said to him, “Put everyone who laps up the water with his tongue, the way a dog laps, in one group. Put everyone who gets down on his knees to drink in another.”",
        "Three hundred men lapped, bringing the water to their mouths with their hands. All the rest of the men got down on their knees to drink.",
        "The Lord said to Gideon, “With the three hundred men who lapped I will save you and hand the Midianites over to you. Let all the others go back home.”",
        "So the men took food and trumpets with them. Gideon sent all the rest of the Israelites home to their tents but kept the three hundred men. The Midianite camp was below him in the valley.",
        "That same night the Lord said to him, “Get up and go down to the camp, because I have handed it over to you.”",
        "“But if you are afraid to attack, go down to the camp with your servant Phurah.”",
        "“Listen to what they are saying, and after that you will have the courage to attack the camp.” So he and his servant Phurah went down to the edge of the camp, where the armed guards were.",
        "The Midianites, the Amalekites, and all the people from the east covered the valley, as many as a swarm of locusts. Their camels could not be counted. There were as many as the grains of sand on the seashore.",
        "Just as Gideon got there, a man was telling his friend about a dream. He said, “I had a dream. A round loaf of barley bread came rolling into the Midianite camp. It hit a tent so hard that the tent fell over, turned upside down, and collapsed.”",
        "His friend answered, “This can only be the sword of Gideon son of Joash, the Israelite! God has handed Midian and its whole army over to him.”",
        "When Gideon heard the dream and what it meant, he bowed down and worshipped. He went back to the camp of Israel and said, “Get up! The Lord has handed the Midianite army over to you.”",
        "He split the three hundred men into three groups. He gave every man a trumpet and an empty clay jar with a torch inside it.",
        "He told them, “Watch me and do what I do. When I get to the edge of the camp, do exactly what I do.”",
        "“When I and everyone with me blow our trumpets, then you blow your trumpets too, all around the camp, and shout, ‘For the Lord and for Gideon!’”",
        "Gideon and the hundred men with him reached the edge of the camp at the start of the middle watch of the night, just after the guards had been changed. They blew their trumpets and smashed the jars they were holding.",
