        "“would you wait for them until they grew up? Would you keep yourselves from marrying for them? No, my daughters. It makes me very sad for you that the Lord’s hand has turned against me.”",
        "Then they cried out loud again. Orpah kissed her mother-in-law goodbye, but Ruth held on to her.",
        "Naomi said, “Look, your sister-in-law has gone back to her people and to her gods. Go back with her.”",
        "But Ruth said, “Don’t beg me to leave you or to stop following you. Where you go, I will go. Where you stay, I will stay. Your people will be my people, and your God will be my God.”",
