        "But one of the young servants told Nabal’s wife Abigail, “Look, David sent messengers from the wilderness to greet our master, but he yelled insults at them.”",
        "“But those men were very good to us. They didn’t harm us, and nothing of ours went missing the whole time we were out in the fields with them.”",
        "“They were like a wall around us night and day, the whole time we were with them taking care of the sheep.”",
        "“So think about it now and decide what to do. Disaster is coming on our master and his whole household. He is such a worthless man (a son of Belial) that no one can talk to him!”",
