        "The Philistines gathered to fight against Israel with thirty thousand chariots, six thousand horsemen, and as many soldiers as the sand on the seashore. They went up and set up camp at Michmash, east of Beth-aven.",
        "When the men of Israel saw what serious trouble they were in, because their army was under heavy pressure, they hid in caves and bushes, among the rocks, in underground rooms, and in pits.",
        "Some of the Hebrews even crossed the Jordan River to the land of Gad and Gilead. But Saul stayed at Gilgal, and all the men with him were shaking with fear.",
        "Saul waited seven days, the time Samuel had set. But Samuel did not come to Gilgal, and the men began to slip away from Saul.",
        "So Saul said, “Bring me the burnt offering and the peace offerings.” And he offered the burnt offering himself.",
        "Just as he finished offering the burnt offering, Samuel arrived. Saul went out to meet him and greet him.",
        "Samuel asked, “What have you done?” Saul answered, “I saw that the men were leaving me, that you didn’t come when you said you would, and that the Philistines were gathering at Michmash.”",
        "I thought, ‘Now the Philistines will come down against me at Gilgal, and I haven’t asked the Lord for His help.’ So I made myself do it, and I offered the burnt offering.",
        "Samuel said to Saul, “You have acted foolishly. You have not kept the commandment the Lord your God gave you. If you had, the Lord would have made your kingdom over Israel last forever.”",
        "But now your kingdom will not last. The Lord has looked for a man after His own heart, and He has chosen him to lead His people, because you have not kept what the Lord commanded you.",
        "Then Samuel got up and left Gilgal and went up to Gibeah in Benjamin. Saul counted the men who were still with him, about six hundred men.",
        "Saul, his son Jonathan, and the men with them stayed in Gibeah of Benjamin, while the Philistines camped at Michmash.",
        "Raiding parties came out of the Philistine camp in three groups. One group headed toward Ophrah, in the land of Shual.",
        "Another group headed toward Beth-horon. The third group headed toward the border that overlooks the valley of Zeboim, toward the desert.",
