        "Naomi had a relative on her husband’s side, a powerful and wealthy man from Elimelech’s clan. His name was Boaz.",
        "Ruth the Moabitess said to Naomi, “Please let me go out to the fields and pick up leftover grain behind someone who will be kind to me.” Naomi told her, “Go, my daughter.”",
        "So she went out to a field and gathered leftover grain behind the harvest workers. As it happened, she ended up in the part of the field that belonged to Boaz, who was from Elimelech’s clan.",
        "Just then Boaz came from Beth-lehem and said to the workers, “The Lord be with you.” They answered him, “The Lord bless you.”",
        "Boaz asked the servant in charge of the workers, “Who does this young woman belong to?”",
        "The servant in charge of the workers answered, “She is the young woman from Moab who came back with Naomi from the land of Moab.”",
        "“She asked, ‘Please let me pick up leftover grain and gather it among the bundles behind the workers.’ So she came, and she has kept at it from early morning until now, except for a short rest in the shelter.”",
        "Then Boaz said to Ruth, “Listen to me, my daughter. Don’t go to gather grain in another field, and don’t leave this one. Stay right here with my young women.”",
        "“Watch which field they are harvesting, and follow along behind them. I have told the young men not to bother you. And when you are thirsty, go to the jars and drink the water the young men have drawn.”",
        "Then she bowed down with her face to the ground and said to him, “Why are you so kind to me? Why do you notice me, when I am a foreigner?”",
        "Boaz answered her, “I have been told all about what you have done for your mother-in-law since your husband died. I know how you left your father and mother and the land where you were born, and came to live among people you did not know before.”",
        "“May the Lord repay you for what you have done. May the Lord God of Israel, under whose wings you have come to find safety, give you a full reward.”",
        "She said, “My lord, may you keep being kind to me. You have comforted me and spoken kindly to me, your servant, even though I am not even one of your own servant girls.”",
        "At mealtime Boaz said to her, “Come over here. Have some bread and dip your piece in the sour wine.” So she sat down beside the workers, and he handed her some roasted grain. She ate until she was full, and she had some left over.",
        "When she got up to gather grain again, Boaz told his young men, “Let her gather even among the bundles, and don’t shame her.”",
        "“Pull out some stalks from the bundles on purpose and leave them for her to pick up. Don’t scold her.”",
        "So she gathered grain in the field until evening. Then she beat the grain loose from what she had gathered, and it came to about an ephah (about half a bushel) of barley.",
        "She picked it up and went into the town, and her mother-in-law saw how much she had gathered. Ruth also took out the food she had saved after she had eaten her fill and gave it to her.",
        "Her mother-in-law asked her, “Where did you gather grain today? Where did you work? Bless the man who noticed you!” So Ruth told her mother-in-law whose field she had worked in. She said, “The name of the man I worked with today is Boaz.”",
        "Naomi said to her daughter-in-law, “May the Lord bless him! The Lord has not stopped being kind to the living or to the dead.” Naomi also told her, “That man is a close relative of ours. He is one of our family redeemers (close relatives who had the right to help and protect the family).”",
        "Then Ruth the Moabitess said, “He also told me, ‘Stay close to my young men until they have finished all my harvest.’”",
        "Naomi said to her daughter-in-law Ruth, “It is good, my daughter, for you to go out with his young women. In another field someone might bother you.”",
        "So Ruth stayed close to Boaz’s young women and gathered grain until the barley harvest and the wheat harvest were over. And she lived with her mother-in-law."
