        "The close relative said, “Then I can’t redeem it for myself, or I would hurt the inheritance I already have. You take my right to redeem it, because I can’t do it.”",
        "In earlier times in Israel, this was how people made a deal final when they redeemed or traded property: one man took off his sandal and gave it to the other. That was how people showed proof of an agreement in Israel.",
