        "As she kept praying to the Lord, Eli watched her mouth.",
        "Hannah was praying silently in her heart. Her lips were moving, but no sound came out. So Eli thought she was drunk.",
        "Eli said to her, “How long are you going to stay drunk? Get rid of your wine!”",
        "Hannah answered, “No, my lord, I am a woman with a heavy heart. I haven’t been drinking wine or beer. I have been pouring out my soul to the Lord.”",
        "“Don’t think your servant is a worthless woman (a daughter of Belial). I have been praying all this time because I am so troubled and hurt.”",
        "Eli answered, “Go in peace. May the God of Israel give you what you have asked Him for.”",
        "She said, “May I, your servant, keep finding kindness in your eyes.” Then she went on her way and ate, and her face was not sad anymore.",
        "Early the next morning they got up and worshipped the Lord. Then they went back home to Ramah. Elkanah slept with his wife Hannah, and the Lord remembered her.",
