        "But Hannah did not go. She told her husband, “Once the boy is weaned (no longer nursing), I will take him to appear before the Lord, and he will stay there for good.”",
        "Her husband Elkanah told her, “Do what you think is best. Stay here until you have weaned him. Only may the Lord do what He has said.” So Hannah stayed home and nursed her son until she weaned him.",
        "When she had weaned him, she took him with her, along with three young bulls, an ephah (about half a bushel) of flour, and a skin bag of wine. She brought him to the house of the Lord at Shiloh, even though he was still very young.",
        "They killed a bull, and they brought the boy to Eli.",
