        "David kept up the chase with four hundred men. Two hundred men stayed behind, because they were too worn out to cross the Besor ravine.",
        "David’s men found an Egyptian out in the open country and brought him to David. They gave him food to eat and water to drink.",
        "They gave him a piece of pressed fig cake and two bunches of raisins. When he had eaten, his strength came back, because he had not had any food or water for three days and three nights.",
        "David asked him, “Who do you belong to, and where are you from?” He said, “I’m a young Egyptian, the servant of an Amalekite. My master left me behind three days ago because I got sick.”",
        "“We raided the south country of the Cherethites, the land that belongs to Judah, and the south country of Caleb. And we burned Ziklag.”",
        "David asked him, “Will you lead me down to this band of raiders?” He said, “Swear to me by God that you won’t kill me or hand me back to my master, and I’ll lead you down to them.”",
        "So he led David down, and there they were, spread out all over the land. They were eating, drinking, and partying because of all the loot they had taken from the land of the Philistines and the land of Judah.",
        "David fought them from dusk until the evening of the next day. Not one of them got away except four hundred young men who rode off on camels.",
        "David got back everything the Amalekites had taken, and he rescued his two wives.",
        "Nothing was missing, small or great, son or daughter, loot or anything else they had taken. David brought it all back.",
        "David also took all the flocks and herds. His men drove them ahead of the other animals and said, “This is David’s prize!”",
        "Then David came back to the two hundred men who had been too worn out to follow him and had been left at the Besor ravine. They came out to meet David and the men with him. When David came near, he greeted them warmly.",
        "But all the evil men and men of Belial (worthless men) among those who had gone with David said, “They didn’t go with us, so we won’t give them any of the loot we got back. Each man can have only his wife and children. Let them take them and leave.”",
        "But David said, “No, my brothers, you must not do that with what the Lord has given us. He has kept us safe and handed over to us the raiders who attacked us.”",
        "“Who would agree with you about this? The share of the man who goes into battle will be the same as the share of the man who stays with the supplies. They will all share alike.”",
        "From that day on, David made this a law and a rule for Israel, and it still is today.",
