        "David sent the people out in three groups: one third under Joab’s command, one third under Abishai son of Zeruiah, Joab’s brother, and one third under Ittai the Gittite (a man from Gath). The king told the people, “I will certainly go out with you myself too.”",
        "But the people said, “You must not go out. If we have to run away, they won’t care about us. Even if half of us die, they won’t care. But you are worth ten thousand of us. So it is better for you to help us from the city.”",
