        "The man answered Joab, “Even if a thousand shekels of silver were weighed out into my hands, I would not lift my hand against the king’s son. We heard the king order you, Abishai, and Ittai, ‘Make sure no one harms the young man Absalom.’”",
        "“Otherwise I would have been acting falsely and risking my own life, because nothing is hidden from the king. And you yourself would have kept your distance from me.”",
        "Joab said, “I’m not going to waste time with you like this.” He took three spears in his hand and drove them into Absalom’s heart while Absalom was still alive in the oak tree.",
        "Then ten young men who carried Joab’s armor surrounded Absalom, struck him, and killed him.",
        "Joab blew the trumpet, and the people came back from chasing Israel, because Joab held the people back.",
        "They took Absalom, threw him into a big pit in the forest, and piled a huge heap of stones over him. And all Israel ran away, every man to his own tent.",
        "While he was alive, Absalom had set up a stone pillar for himself in the King’s Valley. He had said, “I have no son to keep my name remembered.” So he named the pillar after himself, and to this day it is called Absalom’s Place (his monument).",
        "Then Ahimaaz son of Zadok said, “Please let me run and take the news to the king that the Lord has rescued him from his enemies and given him justice.”",
        "But Joab told him, “You are not the one to carry news today. You can carry news another day, but not today, because the king’s son is dead.”",
        "Then Joab said to Cushi, “Go and tell the king what you have seen.” Cushi bowed to Joab and ran off.",
        "Ahimaaz son of Zadok spoke to Joab again: “Whatever happens, please let me run after Cushi too.” Joab said, “Why do you want to run, my son? You have no news that will bring you a reward.”",
        "“Whatever happens,” Ahimaaz said, “let me run.” So Joab told him, “Run.” Then Ahimaaz ran by the road across the plain and got ahead of Cushi.",
        "David was sitting between the two gates. The watchman went up to the roof over the gate, on the wall. He looked out and saw a man running alone.",
        "The watchman called out and told the king. The king said, “If he is alone, he is bringing news.” The man kept coming closer and closer.",
        "Then the watchman saw another man running. He called down to the gatekeeper, “Look, another man is running alone!” The king said, “He is bringing news too.”",
        "The watchman said, “I think the first man runs like Ahimaaz son of Zadok.” The king said, “He is a good man. He is coming with good news.”",
        "Ahimaaz called out to the king, “All is well!” He bowed down before the king with his face to the ground and said, “Praise the Lord your God, who has handed over the men who raised their hands against my lord the king.”",
        "The king asked, “Is the young man Absalom safe?” Ahimaaz answered, “When Joab sent the king’s servant and me, your servant, I saw a big commotion, but I don’t know what it was.”",
