        "The God of Israel spoke. The Rock of Israel said to me: The one who rules over people must be fair and right, ruling with the fear of God.",
        "He will be like the morning light when the sun comes up, a morning with no clouds, like new grass sprouting from the ground when the sun shines after rain.",
        "My family may not be like that before God, but He has made an everlasting covenant with me, arranged in every detail and secure. This is all my salvation and all my desire, even though He does not make it grow.",
        "But the sons of Belial (wicked, worthless men) are all like thorns that get thrown away, because no one can pick them up with bare hands.",
        "Anyone who touches them must be armed with iron or the wooden shaft of a spear. They will be completely burned up with fire right where they are.",
        "These are the names of David’s mighty warriors: The Tachmonite who sat in the seat was the chief of the captains. He was also called Adino the Eznite. He raised his spear against eight hundred men and killed them all at one time.",
        "Next to him was Eleazar son of Dodo the Ahohite. He was one of the three mighty men with David when they challenged the Philistines who had gathered there for battle, and the men of Israel had pulled back.",
        "He stood up and struck down Philistines until his hand was so tired it stuck to the sword. The Lord won a great victory that day. Afterward the people came back to him, but only to take things from the dead.",
        "Next was Shammah son of Agee the Hararite. The Philistines gathered together in a band where there was a field full of lentils (a kind of bean), and Israel’s soldiers ran away from the Philistines.",
        "But Shammah stood his ground in the middle of the field. He defended it and struck down the Philistines, and the Lord won a great victory.",
        "During harvest time, three of the thirty leaders went down to David at the cave of Adullam. A band of Philistines was camped in the valley of Rephaim.",
        "At that time David was in the stronghold, and a troop of Philistine soldiers was in Beth-lehem.",
        "David had a deep longing and said, “If only someone would bring me a drink of water from the well by the gate of Beth-lehem!”",
        "So the three mighty men forced their way through the Philistine camp, drew water from the well by the gate of Beth-lehem, and carried it back to David. But he would not drink it. Instead, he poured it out to the Lord.",
        "He said, “Lord, I could never do this! Isn’t this the blood of the men who risked their lives?” So he would not drink it. These are the things the three mighty men did.",
        "Abishai, the brother of Joab and son of Zeruiah, was the leader of the three. He raised his spear against three hundred men and killed them, and he became famous like the three.",
        "Wasn’t he the most honored of the three? So he became their commander. But he was not one of the first three.",
        "Benaiah son of Jehoiada was the son of a brave man from Kabzeel who did many great deeds. He killed two of Moab’s lion-like warriors. He also went down into a pit on a snowy day and killed a lion.",
        "He killed an Egyptian too, a big, impressive man. The Egyptian had a spear in his hand, but Benaiah went down to fight him with a staff. He grabbed the spear out of the Egyptian’s hand and killed him with his own spear.",
        "These were the brave deeds of Benaiah son of Jehoiada, and he became as famous as the three mighty men.",
        "He was more honored than the thirty, but he was not one of the first three. David put him in charge of his bodyguard.",
        "Asahel, Joab’s brother, was one of the thirty. The others were Elhanan son of Dodo from Beth-lehem,",
        "Shammah the Harodite, and Elika the Harodite,",
        "Helez the Paltite, and Ira son of Ikkesh from Tekoa,",
        "Abiezer the Anethothite, and Mebunnai the Hushathite,",
        "Zalmon the Ahohite, and Maharai the Netophathite,",
        "Heleb son of Baanah, a Netophathite, and Ittai son of Ribai from Gibeah in the land of Benjamin,",
        "Benaiah the Pirathonite, and Hiddai from the streams of Gaash,",
        "Abi-albon the Arbathite, and Azmaveth the Barhumite,",
        "Eliahba the Shaalbonite, and Jonathan from the sons of Jashen,",
        "Shammah the Hararite, and Ahiam son of Sharar the Hararite,",
        "Eliphelet son of Ahasbai, the son of the Maachathite, and Eliam son of Ahithophel the Gilonite,",
        "Hezrai the Carmelite, and Paarai the Arbite,",
        "Igal son of Nathan from Zobah, and Bani the Gadite,",
        "Zelek the Ammonite, and Naharai the Beerothite, who carried the armor for Joab son of Zeruiah,",
        "Ira the Ithrite, and Gareb the Ithrite,",
        "and Uriah the Hittite. There were thirty-seven in all."
