        "He answered, “My lord the king, my servant tricked me. I, your servant, said, ‘I will have a donkey saddled so I can ride it and go with the king,’ because I am lame.”",
        "“And he has told lies about me to my lord the king. But my lord the king is like an angel of God. So do whatever you think is right.”",
        "“All of my father’s family deserved nothing but death from my lord the king. Yet you gave me, your servant, a place among those who eat at your own table. So what right do I have to call out to the king anymore?”",
        "The king said to him, “Why keep talking about your affairs? I have decided: you and Ziba will divide the land.”",
        "Mephibosheth said to the king, “Let him take it all. It is enough that my lord the king has come home safely.”",
        "Barzillai the Gileadite had also come down from Rogelim. He crossed the Jordan with the king to send him on his way across the river.",
        "Barzillai was very old, eighty years old. He had supplied the king with food while the king stayed at Mahanaim, because he was a very rich man.",
        "The king said to Barzillai, “Come across with me, and I will take care of you at my side in Jerusalem.”",
