        "“You know Abner son of Ner. He came to trick you, to find out where you go and where you come from, and to learn everything you are doing.”",
        "Joab left David and sent messengers after Abner. They brought him back from the well of Sirah, but David didn’t know about it.",
        "When Abner got back to Hebron, Joab took him aside into the gateway to talk with him privately. There he stabbed him in the belly, and Abner died. Joab did this to pay him back for the blood of his brother Asahel.",
        "Later, when David heard about it, he said, “I and my kingdom are innocent before the Lord forever of the blood of Abner son of Ner.”",
        "“May his blood fall on the head of Joab and on his father’s whole family. May Joab’s family always have someone with a running sore, or a skin disease like leprosy, or who leans on a cane, or who is killed by the sword, or who has no food.”",
        "So Joab and his brother Abishai killed Abner, because Abner had killed their brother Asahel in the battle at Gibeon.",
        "Then David told Joab and all the people with him, “Tear your clothes, put on sackcloth (rough cloth worn in mourning), and mourn in front of Abner.” King David himself walked behind the bier (the stand that carried the body).",
