        "Joab the son of Zeruiah could tell that the king’s heart longed for Absalom.",
        "So Joab sent someone to Tekoah to bring back a wise woman who lived there. He told her, “Please pretend to be in mourning. Put on mourning clothes, and don’t put any oil on your skin. Act like a woman who has been grieving for someone who died a long time ago.”",
        "“Then go to the king and say this to him.” And Joab told her exactly what to say.",
