        "Then she said, “Please, let the king remember the Lord your God, so that the avenger of blood (the relative who pays back a killing) won’t destroy any more, and they won’t kill my son.” He said, “As surely as the Lord lives, not one hair of your son’s head will fall to the ground.”",
        "Then the woman said, “Please let your servant say one more thing to my lord the king.” He answered, “Go ahead.”",
        "The woman said, “Then why have you planned the same kind of thing against God’s people? By saying what you just said, the king has shown himself to be guilty, because the king has not brought his own banished son back home.”",
        "“All of us must die. We are like water spilled on the ground, which can’t be gathered up again. But God does not take life away. Instead, He makes a way so that the one who is banished doesn’t stay shut out from Him.”",
        "“I have come to say this to my lord the king because the people have frightened me. I, your servant, thought, ‘I will speak to the king. Maybe the king will do what his servant asks.’”",
