        "Then the woman went to all the people with her wise advice. They cut off the head of Sheba son of Bichri and threw it out to Joab. So Joab blew the trumpet, and his men left the city and went home, every man to his tent. And Joab went back to the king in Jerusalem.",
        "Joab was in command of the whole army of Israel. Benaiah son of Jehoiada was in charge of the Cherethites and the Pelethites (the king’s bodyguards).",
