        "In the twelfth year of Ahaz king of Judah, Hoshea son of Elah became king over Israel in Samaria. He ruled for nine years.",
        "He did what the Lord saw as evil, but not as badly as the kings of Israel who came before him.",
        "Shalmaneser king of Assyria came up to attack him. Hoshea became his servant and paid him tribute (money a weaker king pays a stronger one).",
        "But the king of Assyria found out that Hoshea was plotting against him. Hoshea had sent messengers to So king of Egypt, and he had stopped sending tribute to the king of Assyria each year as he used to. So the king of Assyria arrested him and locked him in prison.",
        "Then the king of Assyria invaded the whole land. He marched up to Samaria and surrounded it with his army for three years.",
        "In Hoshea’s ninth year, the king of Assyria captured Samaria and carried the people of Israel off to Assyria. He settled them in Halah, in Habor by the river of Gozan, and in the cities of the Medes.",
        "All this happened because the people of Israel had sinned against the Lord their God. He was the one who had brought them up out of the land of Egypt, out from under the power of Pharaoh king of Egypt. But they worshiped other gods,",
        "and they lived by the customs of the nations the Lord had driven out ahead of the people of Israel, and by the customs the kings of Israel had started.",
        "The people of Israel secretly did things against the Lord their God that were not right. They built high places (shrines) for themselves in all their towns, from the smallest watchtower to the biggest walled city.",
        "They set up sacred stone pillars and Asherah poles (wooden poles for a false goddess) on every high hill and under every leafy tree.",
        "They burned incense there on all the high places, just like the nations the Lord had carried away ahead of them. They did wicked things that made the Lord angry.",
        "They worshiped idols, even though the Lord had told them, “You must not do this.”",
        "Yet the Lord warned Israel and Judah through every prophet and every seer. He said, “Turn away from your evil ways. Keep My commandments and My laws, following the whole law that I commanded your ancestors and that I sent to you through My servants the prophets.”",
        "But they would not listen. They were stubborn, just as stubborn as their ancestors, who did not trust in the Lord their God.",
        "They rejected His laws and the covenant He had made with their ancestors, and the warnings He had given them. They chased after worthless things and became worthless themselves. They copied the nations around them, even though the Lord had commanded them not to act like them.",
        "They abandoned all the commandments of the Lord their God. They made two calves out of melted metal for themselves, and an Asherah pole. They bowed down to all the host of heaven (the sun, moon, and stars) and served Baal.",
        "They made their sons and daughters pass through the fire as offerings. They practiced fortune-telling and magic spells. They gave themselves over to doing evil in the Lord’s sight, making Him angry.",
        "So the Lord was very angry with Israel, and He removed them from His presence. No one was left except the tribe of Judah.",
        "But Judah did not keep the commandments of the Lord their God either. They followed the customs Israel had started.",
        "So the Lord rejected all the descendants of Israel. He brought troubles on them and handed them over to raiders, until He had thrown them out of His sight.",
        "When He tore Israel away from the family of David, they made Jeroboam son of Nebat their king. Jeroboam pulled Israel away from following the Lord and led them into a great sin.",
        "The people of Israel kept on in all the sins Jeroboam had committed. They never turned away from them,",
        "until the Lord removed Israel from His presence, just as He had warned through all His servants the prophets. So Israel was taken from their own land into exile in Assyria, and they are still there today.",
        "The king of Assyria brought people from Babylon, Cuthah, Ava, Hamath, and Sepharvaim. He settled them in the towns of Samaria in place of the people of Israel. They took over Samaria and lived in its towns.",
        "When they first started living there, they did not worship the Lord. So the Lord sent lions among them, and the lions killed some of them.",
        "So someone told the king of Assyria, “The nations you moved and settled in the towns of Samaria don’t know what the God of that land requires. So He has sent lions among them, and the lions are killing them, because they don’t know what the God of the land requires.”",
        "Then the king of Assyria gave this order: “Send back one of the priests you took captive from there. Let them go and live there, and have him teach the people what the God of the land requires.”",
        "So one of the priests who had been carried away from Samaria came and lived in Beth-el. He taught them how they should worship the Lord.",
        "But each nation still made its own gods. They set them up in the shrines on the high places that the Samaritans had built. Each nation did this in the towns where they lived.",
        "The people from Babylon made Succoth-benoth, the people from Cuth made Nergal, the people from Hamath made Ashima,",
        "the Avites made Nibhaz and Tartak, and the Sepharvites burned their children in the fire to Adrammelech and Anammelech, the gods of Sepharvaim.",
        "They worshiped the Lord, but they also chose ordinary people from among themselves to be priests of the high places. These priests offered sacrifices for them in the shrines on the high places.",
        "They worshiped the Lord, but they also served their own gods, following the customs of the nations they had been taken from.",
        "To this day they still follow their old customs. They do not worship the Lord, and they do not keep the laws, rules, teachings, and commandments the Lord gave to the descendants of Jacob, whom He named Israel.",
        "The Lord had made a covenant with them and commanded them, “Do not worship other gods. Do not bow down to them, serve them, or offer sacrifices to them.”",
        "“Instead, worship the Lord, who brought you up out of the land of Egypt with great power and an outstretched arm. He is the one you must honor, bow down to, and offer sacrifices to.”",
        "“Always be careful to keep the laws, rules, teachings, and commandments He wrote for you. Do not worship other gods.”",
        "“Do not forget the covenant I made with you, and do not worship other gods.”",
        "“Worship the Lord your God instead, and He will rescue you from the power of all your enemies.”",
        "But they would not listen. They kept doing things the old way.",
        "So these nations worshiped the Lord, but they also served their carved idols. Their children and grandchildren still do the same today, just as their ancestors did."
