        "So Solomon did what was evil in the Lord’s eyes. He did not follow the Lord all the way, as his father David had.",
        "Then Solomon built a high place (an outdoor worship site) for Chemosh, the disgusting idol of Moab, on the hill facing Jerusalem. He built one for Molech, the disgusting idol of the Ammonites, too.",
        "He did the same for all his foreign wives, who burned incense and offered sacrifices to their gods.",
        "The Lord was angry with Solomon, because his heart had turned away from the Lord, the God of Israel, who had appeared to him two times.",
        "He had commanded Solomon about this very thing: not to follow other gods. But Solomon did not obey what the Lord commanded.",
        "So the Lord said to Solomon, “Because you have done this and have not kept My covenant and My laws that I commanded you, I will surely tear the kingdom away from you and give it to your servant.”",
