        "Earlier, when David was in Edom, Joab the commander of the army had gone up to bury the dead, after he had struck down every male in Edom.",
        "(Joab and all Israel stayed there six months, until he had wiped out every male in Edom.)",
        "But Hadad escaped to Egypt with some Edomites who had served his father. Hadad was still a young boy.",
        "They set out from Midian and came to Paran. They took men from Paran with them and went to Egypt, to Pharaoh king of Egypt. Pharaoh gave Hadad a house, set aside food for him, and gave him land.",
        "Pharaoh liked Hadad so much that he gave him a wife: the sister of his own wife, Queen Tahpenes.",
        "Tahpenes’ sister gave birth to Hadad’s son Genubath. Tahpenes raised the boy in Pharaoh’s palace until he was weaned, and Genubath lived in Pharaoh’s household with Pharaoh’s sons.",
        "While he was in Egypt, Hadad heard that David had died and joined his ancestors, and that Joab the army commander was dead. So Hadad said to Pharaoh, “Let me leave, so I can go back to my own country.”",
        "Pharaoh asked him, “What have you been missing here with me, that you suddenly want to go to your own country?” “Nothing,” Hadad answered, “but please, just let me go.”",
        "God also raised up another enemy against Solomon: Rezon son of Eliadah, who had run away from his master Hadadezer, king of Zobah.",
        "Rezon gathered men around him and became the leader of a band of raiders after David killed the men of Zobah. They went to Damascus, settled there, and ruled in Damascus.",
        "He was Israel’s enemy as long as Solomon lived, adding to the trouble Hadad caused. He hated Israel and ruled over Syria.",
        "Jeroboam son of Nebat also rebelled against the king. He was an Ephrathite (from the tribe of Ephraim) from Zereda and one of Solomon’s officials. His mother was a widow named Zeruah.",
        "This is how he came to rebel against the king. Solomon had built the Millo (raised terraces of packed earth) and closed up the gaps in the wall of the city of his father David.",
        "Jeroboam was a strong and capable man. When Solomon saw how hard the young man worked, he put him in charge of all the forced labor from the house of Joseph.",
        "At that time, as Jeroboam was leaving Jerusalem, the prophet Ahijah the Shilonite (from Shiloh) met him on the road. Ahijah had put on a new cloak, and the two of them were alone out in the country.",
        "Ahijah took hold of the new cloak he was wearing and tore it into twelve pieces.",
        "Then he said to Jeroboam, “Take ten pieces for yourself, because this is what the Lord, the God of Israel, says: I am about to tear the kingdom out of Solomon’s hand, and I will give you ten tribes.”",
        "“But he will keep one tribe, for the sake of My servant David and for the sake of Jerusalem, the city I have chosen out of all the tribes of Israel.”",
        "“I will do this because they have left Me and bowed down to Ashtoreth the goddess of the Zidonians, Chemosh the god of the Moabites, and Milcom the god of the Ammonites. They have not walked in My ways, doing what is right in My eyes and keeping My laws and rules, as his father David did.”",
        "“Even so, I will not take the whole kingdom out of his hand. I will let him rule all the days of his life for the sake of My servant David, whom I chose, because David kept My commandments and My laws.”",
        "“But I will take the kingdom out of his son’s hand and give ten tribes of it to you.”",
        "“I will give his son one tribe, so that My servant David will always have a lamp burning before Me in Jerusalem, the city I chose for Myself to put My name there.”",
        "“As for you, I will take you, and you will rule over everything your heart wants. You will be king over Israel.”",
        "“If you listen to everything I command you, walk in My ways, and do what is right in My eyes by keeping My laws and commandments as My servant David did, then I will be with you. I will build you a lasting family of kings, as I did for David, and I will give Israel to you.”",
        "“Because of this I will bring hardship on David’s descendants, but not forever.”",
        "So Solomon tried to kill Jeroboam. But Jeroboam got up and ran away to Egypt, to Shishak king of Egypt, and he stayed in Egypt until Solomon died.",
        "As for everything else Solomon did, and his wisdom, isn’t it all written in the book of the acts of Solomon?",
