      "ch": "2 Kings 8",
      "verses": [
        "Elisha had spoken to the woman whose son he had brought back to life. He told her, “Get up and go, you and your family, and live for a while wherever you can. The Lord has called for a famine, and it will come on the land for seven years.”",
        "So the woman got up and did what the man of God told her. She and her family went and lived as foreigners in the land of the Philistines for seven years.",
        "At the end of the seven years, the woman came back from the land of the Philistines. She went to the king to plead for her house and her land.",
        "The king was talking with Gehazi, the servant of the man of God. He said, “Please tell me all the great things Elisha has done.”",
        "Gehazi was telling the king how Elisha had brought a dead person back to life. Right then, the woman whose son Elisha had brought back to life came to plead with the king for her house and her land. Gehazi said, “My lord the king, this is the woman, and this is her son whom Elisha brought back to life.”",
        "The king asked the woman, and she told him the story. So the king gave her an official to help her and said, “Give back everything that belonged to her, along with all the crops her field has grown from the day she left the country until now.”",
        "Then Elisha came to Damascus. Ben-hadad the king of Syria was sick, and someone told him, “The man of God has come here.”",
        "The king said to Hazael, “Take a gift with you and go meet the man of God. Ask the Lord through him, ‘Will I get well from this sickness?’”",
        "So Hazael went to meet Elisha. He took a gift with him: every kind of good thing from Damascus, loaded on forty camels. He came and stood in front of Elisha and said, “Your son Ben-hadad king of Syria has sent me to you to ask, ‘Will I get well from this sickness?’”",
        "Elisha answered him, “Go and tell him, ‘You will certainly get well.’ But the Lord has shown me that he will certainly die.”",
        "Elisha stared at him with a steady look until Hazael felt ashamed. Then the man of God began to cry.",
        "Hazael asked, “Why is my lord crying?” Elisha answered, “Because I know the evil you will do to the people of Israel. You will set their forts on fire, kill their young men with the sword, smash their little children, and rip open their pregnant women.”",
        "Hazael said, “How could your servant, who is no more than a dog, do such a huge thing?” Elisha answered, “The Lord has shown me that you will be king over Syria.”",
        "Then Hazael left Elisha and went back to his master. Ben-hadad asked him, “What did Elisha tell you?” He answered, “He told me you will certainly get well.”",
        "But the next day Hazael took a thick cloth, soaked it in water, and spread it over the king’s face, so that he died. Then Hazael became king in his place.",
        "In the fifth year that Joram son of Ahab was king of Israel, while Jehoshaphat was king of Judah, Jehoram son of Jehoshaphat became king of Judah.",
        "He was thirty-two years old when he became king, and he ruled in Jerusalem for eight years.",
        "He followed the ways of the kings of Israel, just like the family of Ahab did, because he had married Ahab’s daughter. He did what was evil in the Lord’s eyes.",
        "Still, the Lord was not willing to destroy Judah, for the sake of His servant David. He had promised to give David and his descendants a lamp forever.",
        "During Jehoram’s time, Edom rebelled against Judah’s rule and made its own king.",
        "So Joram crossed over to Zair with all his chariots. At night he got up and attacked the Edomites who had surrounded him and his chariot captains. But his army ran away to their homes.",
        "So Edom has been in rebellion against Judah’s rule to this day. At that same time Libnah rebelled too.",
        "The rest of what Joram did, and everything he accomplished, is written in the book of the history of the kings of Judah.",
        "Joram died and was buried with his ancestors in the city of David. His son Ahaziah became king in his place.",
        "In the twelfth year that Joram son of Ahab was king of Israel, Ahaziah son of Jehoram became king of Judah.",
        "Ahaziah was twenty-two years old when he became king, and he ruled in Jerusalem for one year. His mother’s name was Athaliah. She was the daughter (meaning descendant) of Omri king of Israel.",
        "He followed the ways of Ahab’s family and did what was evil in the Lord’s eyes, just like Ahab’s family did, because he was related to them by marriage.",
        "Ahaziah went with Joram son of Ahab to fight against Hazael king of Syria at Ramoth-gilead. The Syrians wounded Joram.",
        "So King Joram went back to Jezreel to heal from the wounds the Syrians gave him at Ramah when he fought against Hazael king of Syria. Then Ahaziah son of Jehoram king of Judah went down to Jezreel to visit Joram son of Ahab, because Joram was hurt."
      ],
