        "Rehoboam went to Shechem, because all Israel had gathered at Shechem to make him king.",
        "Jeroboam son of Nebat heard about it while he was still in Egypt. (He had run away from King Solomon, and he had been living in Egypt.)",
        "So they sent for him and called him back. Then Jeroboam and the whole assembly of Israel came and said to Rehoboam,",
        "“Your father put a hard yoke on us. Now make the hard work your father forced on us lighter, and the heavy yoke he put on us, and we will serve you.”",
        "He told them, “Go away for three days, then come back to me.” So the people left.",
        "King Rehoboam asked the advice of the older men who had served his father Solomon while he was alive. “What do you advise?” he asked. “How should I answer these people?”",
        "They told him, “If today you will be a servant to these people and serve them, and answer them with kind words, then they will serve you forever.”",
        "But he rejected the advice the older men gave him. Instead he asked the young men who had grown up with him and now served him.",
        "He asked them, “What do you advise? How should we answer these people? They have told me, ‘Make the yoke your father put on us lighter.’”",
        "The young men who had grown up with him answered, “These people told you, ‘Your father made our yoke heavy, but you make it lighter for us.’ Here is what you should tell them: ‘My little finger is thicker than my father’s waist.’”",
        "“My father loaded a heavy yoke on you, but I will make your yoke even heavier. My father punished you with whips, but I will punish you with scorpions.”",
        "On the third day Jeroboam and all the people came back to Rehoboam, just as the king had told them: “Come back to me on the third day.”",
        "The king answered the people harshly. He rejected the advice the older men had given him",
        "and spoke to them the way the young men had advised. He said, “My father made your yoke heavy, but I will make it even heavier. My father punished you with whips, but I will punish you with scorpions.”",
        "So the king did not listen to the people. This turn of events came from the Lord, to make His word come true, the word the Lord had spoken through Ahijah the Shilonite to Jeroboam son of Nebat.",
        "When all Israel saw that the king would not listen to them, they answered him, “What share do we have in David? We have no inheritance in the son of Jesse! Go home to your tents, Israel! David, now look after your own house!” So the Israelites went home.",
        "But Rehoboam still ruled over the Israelites who lived in the towns of Judah.",
        "Then King Rehoboam sent out Adoram, who was in charge of the forced labor, but all Israel threw stones at him until he died. King Rehoboam rushed to get into his chariot and escaped to Jerusalem.",
        "So Israel has been in rebellion against the house of David to this day.",
        "When all Israel heard that Jeroboam had come back, they sent for him, called him to the assembly, and made him king over all Israel. No one stayed loyal to the house of David except the tribe of Judah.",
        "When Rehoboam got to Jerusalem, he gathered all the house of Judah and the tribe of Benjamin, 180,000 chosen soldiers, to go to war against the house of Israel and win the kingdom back for Rehoboam son of Solomon.",
        "But the word of God came to Shemaiah, the man of God:",
        "“Speak to Rehoboam son of Solomon, king of Judah, and to all the house of Judah and Benjamin, and to the rest of the people. Tell them this:”",
        "“This is what the Lord says: Do not go up and fight against your brothers, the Israelites. Every one of you go back home, because I made this happen.” So they obeyed the word of the Lord and went home, as the Lord had said.",
        "Then Jeroboam built up Shechem in the hill country of Ephraim and lived there. From there he went out and built up Penuel.",
        "Jeroboam thought to himself, “Now the kingdom could go back to the house of David.”",
        "“If these people go up to offer sacrifices at the Lord’s house in Jerusalem, their hearts will turn back to their master, Rehoboam king of Judah. Then they will kill me and go back to Rehoboam king of Judah.”",
        "So after getting advice, the king made two golden calves. He told the people, “It is too much trouble for you to go up to Jerusalem. Look, Israel, here are your gods who brought you up out of the land of Egypt!”",
        "He set up one calf in Beth-el and put the other in Dan.",
        "This became a sin, because the people went all the way to Dan to worship in front of the calf there.",
        "Jeroboam also built shrines on the high places, and he made priests from all sorts of people who were not from the sons of Levi.",
        "Jeroboam started a feast on the fifteenth day of the eighth month, like the feast held in Judah, and he offered sacrifices on the altar. He did this in Beth-el, sacrificing to the calves he had made. He also placed the priests of the high places he had made at Beth-el.",
        "On the fifteenth day of the eighth month, a month he had made up on his own, he offered sacrifices on the altar he had built in Beth-el. He started a feast for the Israelites, and he went up to the altar to burn incense."
