        "The Lord was pleased that Solomon had asked for this.",
        "So God told him, “You asked for this. You did not ask for a long life for yourself, or for riches, or for your enemies to die. Instead you asked for understanding so you can judge fairly.”",
        "“So I will do what you asked. I am giving you a wise and understanding heart. There has never been anyone like you before, and there never will be anyone like you after you.”",
        "“I am also giving you what you did not ask for: riches and honor. As long as you live, no other king will be your equal.”",
        "“And if you walk in My ways and keep My laws and commandments, as your father David did, I will give you a long life.”",
        "Then Solomon woke up and realized it had been a dream. He went to Jerusalem and stood before the ark of the covenant of the Lord. He offered burnt offerings and peace offerings, and he held a feast for all his servants.",
        "Later two women who were prostitutes came to the king and stood in front of him.",
        "One of the women said, “Please, my lord, this woman and I live in the same house. I had a baby while she was there in the house with me.”",
