      "ch": "1 Kings 7",
      "verses": [
        "Solomon spent thirteen years building his own palace, and then he finished the whole palace.",
        "He also built the House of the Forest of Lebanon (a great hall built with cedar from Lebanon). It was a hundred cubits long, fifty cubits wide, and thirty cubits high, and it stood on four rows of cedar pillars with cedar beams on top of the pillars.",
        "It had a cedar roof above the beams that rested on forty-five pillars, fifteen in each row.",
        "There were windows set in three rows, with window facing window in three tiers.",
        "All the doorways and doorposts had square frames, and the windows faced each other in three tiers.",
        "He made a hall of pillars fifty cubits long and thirty cubits wide. In front of it was a porch, with pillars and a covering in front of them.",
        "Then he made the hall for the throne where he would judge, the Hall of Judgment. It was lined with cedar from one side of the floor to the other.",
        "The palace where he lived, in another courtyard set back from the hall, was built the same way. Solomon also built a house like this hall for Pharaoh’s daughter, whom he had married.",
        "All these buildings were made of costly stones, cut to size and trimmed with saws on the inside and outside, from the foundation all the way up to the top edge, and on the outside out to the great courtyard.",
        "The foundations were laid with costly stones, big stones, some ten cubits long and some eight cubits long.",
        "Above them were costly stones cut to size, and cedar beams.",
        "The great courtyard all around had three rows of cut stone and one row of cedar beams, the same as the inner courtyard of the house of the Lord and the porch of the house.",
        "King Solomon sent for Hiram and brought him from Tyre.",
        "Hiram was the son of a widow from the tribe of Naphtali, and his father was a man from Tyre who worked in bronze. Hiram was full of wisdom, understanding, and skill to do every kind of bronze work. He came to King Solomon and did all his work.",
        "He cast two bronze pillars, each eighteen cubits tall, and it took a cord twelve cubits long to go around each one.",
        "He also made two capitals (decorated tops) of cast bronze to set on top of the pillars. Each capital was five cubits high.",
        "For the capitals on top of the pillars he made nets of crisscross work and wreaths of chain work, seven for one capital and seven for the other.",
        "He made the pillars with two rows of pomegranates all around on each network, to cover the capitals on top. He did the same for the other capital.",
        "The capitals on top of the pillars in the porch were shaped like lilies, four cubits high.",
        "On the capitals of both pillars, above the rounded part next to the network, there were also pomegranates: two hundred of them in rows all around, on the other capital as well.",
        "He set up the pillars at the porch of the temple. He set up the right-hand pillar and named it Jachin, and he set up the left-hand pillar and named it Boaz.",
        "The tops of the pillars were shaped like lilies. So the work on the pillars was done.",
        "He made the Sea, a huge round basin of cast metal. It measured ten cubits from rim to rim and five cubits high, and a cord of thirty cubits went all the way around it.",
        "Below its rim, all the way around, were gourd-shaped knobs, ten to each cubit, circling the Sea. The knobs were cast in two rows as part of the Sea itself.",
        "It stood on twelve oxen: three faced north, three faced west, three faced south, and three faced east. The Sea rested on top of them, and all their back ends pointed inward.",
        "It was as thick as the width of a hand, and its rim was shaped like the rim of a cup, like a lily flower. It held two thousand baths (a bath is about six gallons).",
        "He also made ten bronze stands. Each stand was four cubits long, four cubits wide, and three cubits high.",
        "This is how the stands were made: they had side panels, and the panels were set between frames.",
        "On the panels between the frames were lions, oxen, and cherubim. On the frames there was a stand above, and below the lions and oxen were hanging wreaths.",
        "Each stand had four bronze wheels with bronze axles. Its four corners had supports cast underneath the basin, with wreaths at the side of each.",
        "Its opening inside the crown at the top was a cubit high. The opening was round, made like a pedestal, a cubit and a half across. Around its opening there were carvings, and its panels were square, not round.",
        "The four wheels were under the panels, and the axles of the wheels were attached to the stand. Each wheel was a cubit and a half tall.",
        "The wheels were made like chariot wheels. Their axles, rims, spokes, and hubs were all cast metal.",
        "There were four supports at the four corners of each stand, made in one piece with the stand.",
        "At the top of the stand was a round band half a cubit high. The frames and panels on top of the stand were made in one piece with it.",
        "On the surfaces of its frames and panels he carved cherubim, lions, and palm trees, wherever there was room for each, with wreaths all around.",
        "This is how he made the ten stands. They were all cast the same way, with the same measurements and the same shape.",
        "Then he made ten bronze basins. Each basin held forty baths and was four cubits across. There was one basin on each of the ten stands.",
        "He put five stands on the right side of the house and five on the left side. He set the Sea on the right side of the house, toward the southeast.",
        "Hiram also made the lavers (washbasins), the shovels, and the bowls. So Hiram finished all the work he did for King Solomon for the house of the Lord:",
        "the two pillars; the two bowl-shaped capitals on top of the two pillars; the two networks covering the two bowls of the capitals on top of the pillars;",
        "the four hundred pomegranates for the two networks, two rows of pomegranates for each network, covering the two bowls of the capitals on the pillars;",
        "the ten stands, and the ten basins on the stands;",
        "the one Sea, and the twelve oxen under the Sea;",
        "and the pots, the shovels, and the bowls. All these things that Hiram made for King Solomon for the house of the Lord were made of polished bronze.",
        "The king had them cast in clay molds in the plain of the Jordan, between Succoth and Zarthan.",
        "Solomon did not weigh any of these things, because there were so very many. No one ever found out how much the bronze weighed.",
        "Solomon also made all the things that belonged in the house of the Lord: the gold altar, and the gold table that held the showbread (the holy bread set out before the Lord);",
        "the lampstands of pure gold, five on the right and five on the left, in front of the inner sanctuary; and the gold flowers, lamps, and tongs;",
        "the bowls, the wick trimmers, the basins, the spoons, and the fire pans, all of pure gold; and the gold hinges for the doors of the inner room, the most holy place, and for the doors of the main hall of the temple.",
        "So all the work King Solomon did for the house of the Lord was finished. Then Solomon brought in the things his father David had set apart as holy: the silver, the gold, and the dishes. He put them in the treasuries of the house of the Lord."
      ],
