        "In the ninth year of Zedekiah’s rule, on the tenth day of the tenth month, Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came with his whole army to attack Jerusalem. They camped around the city and built siege walls all around it.",
        "The city stayed surrounded until King Zedekiah’s eleventh year.",
        "By the ninth day of the fourth month, the hunger in the city was so bad that the people of the land had no food at all.",
