        "But the army of the Chaldees (Babylonians) chased the king and caught him on the plains near Jericho. All his soldiers scattered and left him.",
        "They captured the king and took him to the king of Babylon at Riblah, and there they decided his punishment.",
        "They killed Zedekiah’s sons while he watched. Then they blinded Zedekiah, put him in bronze chains, and took him to Babylon.",
        "On the seventh day of the fifth month, in the nineteenth year of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, Nebuzar-adan came to Jerusalem. He was the commander of the guard and an officer of the king of Babylon.",
        "He burned down the Lord’s temple, the king’s palace, and all the houses of Jerusalem. He set fire to every important building.",
        "The whole army of the Chaldees, who were with the commander of the guard, tore down the walls all around Jerusalem.",
        "Nebuzar-adan, the commander of the guard, took away as captives the rest of the people left in the city, the people who had already gone over to the king of Babylon’s side, and the rest of the crowd.",
        "But the commander of the guard left some of the poorest people of the land to work in the vineyards and farm the fields.",
        "The Chaldees broke up the bronze pillars, the stands, and the huge bronze water basin called the Sea that were in the Lord’s temple. They carried the bronze to Babylon.",
        "They also took the pots, shovels, wick trimmers, dishes, and all the bronze tools used for the temple service.",
        "The commander of the guard took the fire pans and the bowls, whatever was made of gold or of silver.",
        "As for the two pillars, the one Sea, and the stands Solomon had made for the Lord’s temple, the bronze in all these things was too much to weigh.",
        "Each pillar was eighteen cubits tall (about 27 feet). The bronze top on it was three cubits high, with bronze netting and pomegranates all around it. The second pillar, with its netting, was just like it.",
        "The commander of the guard also took Seraiah the chief priest, Zephaniah the next priest in rank, and the three doorkeepers.",
        "From the city he took an officer who was in charge of the soldiers, and five of the king’s advisers who were found in the city. He took the scribe of the army commander, who signed up the people of the land for the army, and sixty men of the people of the land who were found in the city.",
        "Nebuzar-adan, the commander of the guard, took them and brought them to the king of Babylon at Riblah.",
        "There at Riblah, in the land of Hamath, the king of Babylon had them struck down and killed. So Judah was taken away from its land as captives.",
        "Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon put Gedaliah son of Ahikam, son of Shaphan, in charge of the people he had left behind in the land of Judah.",
        "All the army commanders and their men heard that the king of Babylon had made Gedaliah governor. So they came to Gedaliah at Mizpah: Ishmael son of Nethaniah, Johanan son of Careah, Seraiah son of Tanhumeth the Netophathite, and Jaazaniah son of the Maachathite, with their men.",
        "Gedaliah made a promise with an oath to them and their men. He told them, “Don’t be afraid to serve the Chaldees. Stay in the land and serve the king of Babylon, and things will go well for you.”",
        "But in the seventh month, Ishmael son of Nethaniah, son of Elishama, who was from the royal family, came with ten men. They attacked and killed Gedaliah, along with the Jews and the Chaldees who were with him at Mizpah.",
        "Then all the people, from the least to the greatest, and the army commanders got up and went to Egypt, because they were afraid of the Chaldees.",
        "In the thirty-seventh year after Jehoiachin king of Judah was taken captive, on the twenty-seventh day of the twelfth month, Evil-merodach king of Babylon, in the year he became king, showed favor to Jehoiachin king of Judah and let him out of prison.",
