        "David looked up and saw the angel of the Lord standing between earth and heaven, holding a drawn sword stretched out over Jerusalem. Then David and the elders of Israel, who were dressed in sackcloth (rough cloth worn in sorrow), bowed down with their faces to the ground.",
        "David said to God, “Wasn’t I the one who ordered the people to be counted? I am the one who sinned and did this terrible wrong. But these people are like sheep. What have they done? Lord my God, please let Your hand strike me and my father’s family, but don’t keep this plague on Your people.”",
