        "Then all the people of Israel came together to David at Hebron. They said, “Look, we are your own flesh and blood.”",
        "“Even in the past, when Saul was king, you were the one who led Israel out to battle and brought them home again. And the Lord your God told you, ‘You will be the shepherd of My people Israel, and you will be the ruler over My people Israel.’”",
        "So all the leaders of Israel came to the king at Hebron. There David made a covenant with them in front of the Lord, and they anointed David king over Israel, just as the Lord had promised through Samuel.",
        "Then David and all Israel marched to Jerusalem, which was then called Jebus. The Jebusites, who lived in that land, were there.",
        "The people of Jebus told David, “You will never get in here.” But David captured the fortress of Zion, which is the city of David.",
        "David had said, “Whoever attacks the Jebusites first will become the head commander.” Joab son of Zeruiah was the first to go up, so he became the commander.",
        "David made his home in the fortress, and that is why it was named the city of David.",
        "He built up the city all around it, starting from the Millo (a raised platform of earth and stone). Joab rebuilt the rest of the city.",
        "David kept growing stronger and stronger, because the Lord of Hosts was with him.",
        "These were the leaders of David’s mighty warriors. Along with all Israel, they gave strong support to his rule and helped make him king, just as the Lord had promised about Israel.",
        "Here is the list of David’s mighty warriors: Jashobeam, a Hachmonite, was head of the officers. He used his spear against three hundred men and killed them all in one battle.",
        "Next came Eleazar son of Dodo, the Ahohite. He was one of the three greatest warriors.",
        "He was with David at Pas-dammim when the Philistines gathered there to fight. There was a field there full of barley, and the Israelite soldiers ran away from the Philistines.",
        "But they took their stand in the middle of that field and held onto it. They struck down the Philistines, and the Lord saved them with a great victory.",
        "Three of the thirty chief warriors came down to the rock where David was, at the cave of Adullam. Meanwhile, the Philistine army was camped in the valley of Rephaim.",
        "At that time David was in the fortress, and a group of Philistine soldiers was stationed in Beth-lehem.",
        "David felt a deep longing and said, “If only someone would bring me a drink of water from the well by the gate of Beth-lehem!”",
        "So the three warriors forced their way through the Philistine camp, drew water from the well by the gate of Beth-lehem, and carried it back to David. But David refused to drink it. Instead, he poured it out as an offering to the Lord.",
        "He said, “My God, I could never do such a thing! Should I drink the blood of these men who risked their lives? They put their lives in danger to bring it.” So he would not drink it. These were the brave deeds of the three mighty warriors.",
        "Abishai, Joab’s brother, was the leader of the three. He used his spear against three hundred men and killed them, and he became famous along with the three.",
        "He was honored more than the other two of the three, and he became their commander. But he was not counted among the first three.",
        "Benaiah son of Jehoiada was the son of a brave man from Kabzeel who did many great deeds. He killed two of Moab’s mightiest warriors (men like lions). He also went down into a pit on a snowy day and killed a lion.",
        "He killed an Egyptian too, a huge man five cubits (about seven and a half feet) tall. The Egyptian held a spear as thick as the beam of a weaver’s loom. Benaiah went against him with just a club, grabbed the spear out of his hand, and killed him with it.",
        "Those were the brave deeds of Benaiah son of Jehoiada. He became as famous as the three mighty warriors.",
        "He was honored more than the thirty, but he was not one of the first three. David put him in charge of his bodyguard.",
        "The brave warriors of the army were: Asahel, Joab’s brother; Elhanan son of Dodo from Beth-lehem;",
        "Shammoth, a Harorite; Helez, a Pelonite;",
        "Ira son of Ikkesh, a Tekoite; Abi-ezer, an Antothite;",
        "Sibbecai, a Hushathite; Ilai, an Ahohite;",
        "Maharai, a Netophathite; Heled son of Baanah, also a Netophathite;",
        "Ithai son of Ribai from Gibeah in Benjamin’s land; Benaiah, a Pirathonite;",
        "Hurai from the streams of Gaash; Abiel, an Arbathite;",
        "Azmaveth, a Baharumite; Eliahba, a Shaalbonite;",
        "Hashem the Gizonite’s sons; Jonathan son of Shage, a Hararite;",
        "Ahiam son of Sacar, a Hararite; Eliphal son of Ur;",
        "Hepher, a Mecherathite; Ahijah, a Pelonite;",
        "Hezro, a Carmelite; Naarai son of Ezbai;",
        "Joel, Nathan’s brother; Mibhar son of Haggeri;",
        "Zelek, an Ammonite; Naharai, a Berothite, who carried the weapons of Joab son of Zeruiah;",
        "Ira, an Ithrite; Gareb, another Ithrite;",
        "Uriah, a Hittite; Zabad son of Ahlai;",
        "Adina son of Shiza, a Reubenite, who was a leader of the Reubenites, with thirty men alongside him;",
        "Hanan son of Maachah; Joshaphat, a Mithnite;",
        "Uzzia, an Ashterathite; Shama and Jehiel, sons of Hothan, an Aroerite;",
        "Jediael son of Shimri, and his brother Joha, a Tizite;",
        "Eliel, a Mahavite; Jeribai and Joshaviah, Elnaam’s sons; Ithmah, a Moabite;",
        "Eliel, Obed, and Jasiel, a Mesobaite."
