        "Next to them, the people of Gad lived in Bashan, as far as Salchah.",
        "Joel was their leader, Shapham was second, and then came Jaanai and Shaphat, there in Bashan.",
        "Their relatives, by family, were seven men: Michael, Meshullam, Sheba, Jorai, Jachan, Zia, and Heber.",
        "They were descended from Abihail. His father was Huri, whose father was Jaroah, whose father was Gilead, whose father was Michael, whose father was Jeshishai, whose father was Jahdo, whose father was Buz.",
        "Ahi, whose father was Abdiel, whose father was Guni, was head of their family.",
        "They lived in Gilead, in Bashan and its towns, and in all the grasslands of Sharon, out to their edges.",
        "All of them were written in the family records while Jotham ruled Judah and Jeroboam ruled Israel.",
        "Reuben’s tribe, Gad’s tribe, and half of Manasseh’s tribe had 44,760 brave soldiers ready for battle. They could carry a shield and sword, shoot a bow, and were trained to fight.",
        "They went to war against the Hagarites, Jetur, Nephish, and Nodab.",
        "They were helped in fighting their enemies, and the Hagarites and everyone with them were handed over to them. That happened because they cried out to God during the battle, and He answered their prayer, since they trusted in Him.",
        "They captured the enemy’s animals: 50,000 camels, 250,000 sheep, and 2,000 donkeys. They also took 100,000 people captive.",
