        "Some time later, David attacked the Philistines and brought them under his control. He took Gath and the villages around it away from the Philistines.",
        "He also defeated Moab, and the Moabites came under David’s rule and paid him tribute (money or goods owed to a ruler).",
        "David also defeated Hadarezer king of Zobah as far as Hamath, when he went to set up his rule along the Euphrates River.",
        "David captured a thousand chariots, seven thousand horsemen, and twenty thousand soldiers on foot from him. David crippled all the chariot horses by cutting their leg tendons, but he kept enough for a hundred chariots.",
        "When the Syrians from Damascus came to help Hadarezer king of Zobah, David killed twenty-two thousand of the Syrian men.",
        "Then David stationed troops in Syria-damascus, and the Syrians came under David’s rule and paid him tribute. The Lord gave David victory everywhere he went.",
        "David took the gold shields that Hadarezer’s officers carried and brought them to Jerusalem.",
        "From Tibhath and Chun, cities that belonged to Hadarezer, David also took a huge amount of bronze. Solomon later used it to make the bronze sea (a giant water basin), the pillars, and the bronze tools.",
