        "Elkanah, Jesiah, Azareel, Joezer, Jashobeam, who were Korhites;",
        "plus Joelah and Zebadiah, sons of Jeroham from Gedor.",
        "Some men from Gad left their own people and joined David at his fortress in the wilderness. They were strong, brave men, trained for war, skilled with shield and spear. Their faces looked like lions’ faces, and they ran as fast as gazelles on the mountains.",
        "Ezer was in first place, Obadiah in second, Eliab in third,",
        "Mishmannah in fourth, Jeremiah in fifth,",
        "Attai in sixth, Eliel in seventh,",
        "Johanan in eighth, Elzabad in ninth,",
        "Jeremiah in tenth, Machbanai in eleventh.",
        "These men from Gad were army officers. The least of them led a hundred men, and the greatest led a thousand.",
        "They were the ones who crossed the Jordan River in the first month of the year, when it was flooding over all its banks. They chased away everyone living in the valleys, to the east and to the west.",
        "Some men from Benjamin and Judah also came to David at his fortress.",
        "David went out to meet them and told them, “If you have come in peace to help me, I will join my heart with yours. But if you have come to hand me over to my enemies, even though I have done nothing wrong, may the God of our fathers see it and punish you.”",
        "Then the Spirit came over Amasai, the leader of the officers, and he said, “We belong to you, David! We are on your side, son of Jesse! Peace, peace to you, and peace to everyone who helps you, for your God is helping you.” So David welcomed them and made them officers over his fighting band.",
        "Some men from Manasseh also switched sides and joined David when he went with the Philistines to fight against Saul. But David and his men did not end up helping the Philistines. After talking it over, the Philistine rulers sent him away. They said, “If he goes back to his master Saul, it will cost us our heads.”",
        "When David went to Ziklag, these men from Manasseh came over to his side: Adnah, Jozabad, Jediael, Michael, Jozabad, Elihu, and Zilthai. Each was a commander of a thousand men in Manasseh.",
        "They helped David fight against the bands of raiders, because they were all brave, strong warriors, and they were commanders in the army.",
        "Day after day men kept coming to help David, until he had a huge army, like the army of God.",
        "Here are the numbers of the armed soldiers ready for war who came to David at Hebron to turn Saul’s kingdom over to him, just as the Lord had said:",
        "From Judah came 6,800 men carrying shields and spears, armed and ready for war.",
        "From Simeon came 7,100 brave warriors ready for battle.",
        "From Levi came 4,600.",
        "Jehoiada was the leader of Aaron’s family, and 3,700 men came with him.",
        "Zadok, a brave young warrior, came too, along with 22 officers from his father’s family.",
        "From Benjamin, Saul’s own relatives, came 3,000. Until then, most of them had stayed loyal to Saul’s family.",
        "From Ephraim came 20,800 brave warriors, men who were famous in their own families.",
        "From half the tribe of Manasseh came 18,000, chosen by name to come and make David king.",
        "From Issachar came men who understood the times and knew what Israel should do. There were 200 leaders, and all their relatives followed their orders.",
        "From Zebulun came 50,000 soldiers ready for battle, trained to fight with every kind of weapon. They could hold their battle lines, and they were loyal with their whole heart.",
        "From Naphtali came 1,000 officers, along with 37,000 men carrying shields and spears.",
        "From Dan came 28,600 men trained for battle.",
        "From Asher came 40,000 soldiers ready to march out and fight.",
        "From the far side of the Jordan River, from Reuben, Gad, and half the tribe of Manasseh, came 120,000 men armed with every kind of weapon.",
        "All these fighting men, ready in their battle lines, came to Hebron fully committed to making David king over all Israel. All the rest of Israel also agreed together to make David king.",
