        "But Jehoshaphat asked, “Isn’t there still a prophet of the Lord here we could ask?”",
        "The king of Israel answered Jehoshaphat, “There is still one man we could ask to learn what the Lord says, but I hate him. He never prophesies anything good about me, only bad things. He is Micaiah son of Imla.” Jehoshaphat said, “The king shouldn’t say that.”",
        "So the king of Israel called one of his officials and said, “Bring Micaiah son of Imla right away.”",
        "The king of Israel and Jehoshaphat king of Judah were each sitting on his throne, dressed in their royal robes. They sat at the threshing floor (a flat, open place) by the entrance to the gate of Samaria, and all the prophets were prophesying in front of them.",
        "Zedekiah son of Chenaanah had made himself horns out of iron. He said, “This is what the Lord says: ‘With these you will gore the Syrians until they are wiped out.’”",
        "All the prophets were prophesying the same thing. They said, “Go up to Ramoth-gilead and win, because the Lord will give it into the king’s power.”",
        "The messenger who went to call Micaiah told him, “Look, the prophets all agree and are saying good things to the king. So please make your message like theirs, and say something good.”",
        "But Micaiah said, “As surely as the Lord lives, I will say whatever my God tells me.”",
        "When he came to the king, the king asked him, “Micaiah, should we go to war against Ramoth-gilead, or should I hold back?” He answered, “Go up and win. They will be handed over to you.”",
        "The king said to him, “How many times do I have to make you swear to tell me nothing but the truth in the name of the Lord?”",
        "Then Micaiah said, “I saw all Israel scattered on the mountains like sheep with no shepherd. And the Lord said, ‘These people have no master. Let each of them go home in peace.’”",
        "The king of Israel said to Jehoshaphat, “Didn’t I tell you he would never prophesy anything good about me, only bad?”",
        "Micaiah went on, “So listen to the word of the Lord. I saw the Lord sitting on His throne, and all the armies of heaven were standing on His right and on His left.”",
        "“The Lord asked, ‘Who will trick Ahab king of Israel into going up to Ramoth-gilead so he will die there?’ One said one thing, and another said something else.”",
        "“Then a spirit came forward and stood before the Lord. It said, ‘I will trick him.’ The Lord asked it, ‘How?’”",
        "“It said, ‘I will go out and be a lying spirit in the mouths of all his prophets.’ The Lord said, ‘You will trick him, and you will succeed. Go and do it.’”",
        "“So now you see, the Lord has put a lying spirit in the mouths of these prophets of yours. The Lord has announced disaster for you.”",
        "Then Zedekiah son of Chenaanah walked up and slapped Micaiah on the cheek. He said, “Which way did the Spirit of the Lord go when He left me to speak to you?”",
        "Micaiah answered, “You will find out on the day you go into an inner room to hide.”",
        "Then the king of Israel said, “Take Micaiah and send him back to Amon, the governor of the city, and to Joash, the king’s son.”",
        "“Tell them, ‘This is what the king says: Put this man in prison. Give him nothing but a little bread and water until I come back safely.’”",
