        "Josiah held a Passover for the Lord in Jerusalem. They killed the Passover lambs on the fourteenth day of the first month.",
        "He gave the priests their duties and encouraged them in their work in the house of the Lord.",
        "He said to the Levites, who taught all Israel and were set apart as holy to the Lord, “Put the holy ark in the house that Solomon son of David, king of Israel, built. You will no longer have to carry it on your shoulders. Now serve the Lord your God and His people Israel.”",
        "“Get yourselves ready by your family groups, in your divisions, the way David king of Israel and his son Solomon wrote down.”",
        "“Stand in the holy place by the family groups of your fellow Israelites, the people, with a group of Levite families for each one.”",
        "“Kill the Passover lambs, make yourselves holy, and get things ready for your brothers, so they can do what the Lord commanded through Moses.”",
        "Josiah gave the people animals from the flock, lambs and young goats, all for the Passover offerings for everyone there, thirty thousand in all, plus three thousand bulls. These came from the king’s own herds and flocks.",
        "His officials also gave freely to the people, the priests, and the Levites. Hilkiah, Zechariah, and Jehiel, the leaders of the house of God, gave the priests two thousand six hundred sheep and goats for the Passover offerings, and three hundred oxen.",
        "Conaniah, with his brothers Shemaiah and Nethaneel, and Hashabiah, Jeiel, and Jozabad, the leaders of the Levites, gave the Levites five thousand sheep and goats for the Passover offerings, and five hundred oxen.",
        "So everything for the service was ready. The priests stood in their places, and the Levites stood in their divisions, just as the king had commanded.",
        "They killed the Passover lambs. The priests sprinkled the blood they were handed, while the Levites skinned the animals.",
        "They set aside the burnt offerings to give to the family groups of the people, so they could offer them to the Lord as it is written in the book of Moses. They did the same with the oxen.",
        "They roasted the Passover lambs over the fire, as the law said. They boiled the other holy offerings in pots, kettles, and pans, and quickly handed them out to all the people.",
        "After that, they got food ready for themselves and for the priests, because the priests, the sons of Aaron, were busy offering the burnt offerings and the fat until night. So the Levites prepared food for themselves and for the priests, the sons of Aaron.",
        "The singers, the sons of Asaph, were at their posts, as David, Asaph, Heman, and Jeduthun the king’s seer had commanded. The gatekeepers stayed at each gate. They did not have to leave their work, because their fellow Levites prepared food for them.",
        "So all the Lord’s service was carried out that day, to keep the Passover and to offer burnt offerings on the altar of the Lord, as King Josiah had commanded.",
        "The people of Israel who were there kept the Passover at that time, and the Feast of Unleavened Bread for seven days.",
        "No Passover like this one had been held in Israel since the days of Samuel the prophet. None of the kings of Israel had ever held a Passover like the one Josiah held with the priests, the Levites, all Judah, the Israelites who were there, and the people of Jerusalem.",
        "This Passover was held in the eighteenth year that Josiah was king.",
        "After all this, when Josiah had set the temple in order, Necho king of Egypt came up to fight at Carchemish by the Euphrates River, and Josiah went out to meet him in battle.",
        "But Necho sent messengers to him to say, “What do you and I have to do with each other, king of Judah? I am not coming against you today, but against the house I am at war with. God has told me to hurry. Stop fighting against God, who is with me, or He will destroy you.”",
        "But Josiah would not turn back from him. He put on a disguise so he could fight him. He did not listen to what Necho said, though it came from the mouth of God, and he went to fight in the valley of Megiddo.",
        "Archers shot King Josiah, and the king told his servants, “Get me out of here, for I am badly wounded.”",
        "So his servants took him out of that chariot, put him in his second chariot, and brought him to Jerusalem. There he died, and he was buried in one of the tombs of his fathers. All Judah and Jerusalem mourned for Josiah.",
        "Jeremiah sang a lament (a song of grief) for Josiah. To this day all the men and women singers speak of Josiah in their laments. They made this a custom in Israel, and the laments are written in the book of laments.",
