        "This happened in the days of Ahasuerus (the Persian king also called Xerxes). This Ahasuerus ruled over 127 provinces, from India all the way to Ethiopia.",
        "In those days King Ahasuerus sat on his royal throne in Shushan, the fortress city.",
        "In the third year that he was king, he gave a feast for all his officials and servants. The army leaders of Persia and Media, the nobles, and the governors of the provinces were there with him.",
        "For a long time, 180 days in all, he showed off the riches of his glorious kingdom and the splendor and honor of his greatness.",
        "When those days were over, the king gave a feast for all the people in Shushan, the fortress city, from the most important to the least. It lasted seven days and was held in the courtyard of the garden of the king’s palace.",
        "There were white, green, and blue curtains, tied with cords of fine linen and purple cloth to silver rings and marble pillars. There were couches of gold and silver on a floor laid with red, blue, white, and black stone.",
        "Drinks were served in gold cups, and every cup was different from the others. There was plenty of royal wine, as you would expect from a generous king.",
        "The rule for the drinking was that no one had to drink. The king had told all the servants of his palace to give each guest whatever he wanted.",
        "Queen Vashti also gave a feast for the women in King Ahasuerus’s royal palace.",
        "On the seventh day, when the king was feeling happy from the wine, he gave an order to the seven chamberlains (his palace servants) who served King Ahasuerus: Mehuman, Biztha, Harbona, Bigtha, Abagtha, Zethar, and Carcas.",
        "He told them to bring Queen Vashti to him wearing her royal crown, so he could show off her beauty to the people and the officials. She was very beautiful.",
        "But Queen Vashti refused to come when the servants brought her the king’s order. The king became very angry, and his rage burned inside him.",
        "The king spoke with the wise men who understood the times. (This was how the king did things: he asked the advice of all who were experts in law and justice.",
        "His closest advisers were Carshena, Shethar, Admatha, Tarshish, Meres, Marsena, and Memucan. They were the seven princes of Persia and Media who could meet with the king face to face and who held the highest places in the kingdom.)",
        "The king asked, “What does the law say we should do to Queen Vashti, since she did not obey the order King Ahasuerus sent by his servants?”",
        "Memucan answered in front of the king and the princes, “Queen Vashti has not just wronged the king. She has wronged all the princes and all the people in every province of King Ahasuerus.”",
        "What the queen did will become known to all the women, and they will look down on their husbands. They will say, “King Ahasuerus ordered Queen Vashti to be brought to him, but she would not come.”",
        "This very day the noble ladies of Persia and Media who have heard what the queen did will say the same thing to all the king’s officials. There will be no end of disrespect and anger.",
        "So if the king agrees, let him send out a royal order. Let it be written into the laws of the Persians and the Medes, which can never be changed, that Vashti may never again come before King Ahasuerus. And let the king give her place as queen to another woman who is better than she is.",
        "When the king’s order is announced all through his huge kingdom, all the wives will honor their husbands, from the most important to the least.",
        "The king and the princes liked this advice, so the king did what Memucan said.",
