        "So the king and Haman went to the feast with Queen Esther.",
        "On this second day, while they were drinking wine at the feast, the king asked Esther again, “Queen Esther, what do you want to ask? It will be given to you. What is your request? Even up to half the kingdom, it will be done.”",
        "Then Queen Esther answered, “If you are pleased with me, my king, and if it pleases the king, spare my life. That is what I ask. And spare my people. That is my request.”",
        "“For I and my people have been sold to be destroyed, killed, and wiped out. If we had only been sold as slaves, men and women, I would have kept quiet. But the enemy could never make up for the loss this would cause the king.”",
        "Then King Ahasuerus said to Queen Esther, “Who is he? Where is the man who has dared to plan such a thing?”",
