        "Just then the king came back from the palace garden into the room where they were drinking wine. Haman had thrown himself down on the couch where Esther was lying. The king said, “Will he even attack the queen while I am right here in the house?” As soon as the king said this, they covered Haman’s face.",
        "Then Harbonah, one of the chamberlains serving the king, said, “Look, there is a pole for hanging, fifty cubits high (about 75 feet), standing at Haman’s house. Haman made it for Mordecai, the man who spoke up and saved the king.” The king said, “Hang him on it!”",
