        "In the month of Nisan, in the twentieth year of King Artaxerxes, wine was set in front of him. I picked up the wine and handed it to the king. I had never looked sad in front of him before.",
        "So the king asked me, “Why do you look so sad when you aren’t sick? This can only be sadness of heart.” Then I was terribly afraid.",
