        "Then I told the king, “If it pleases the king, and if your servant has won your approval, send me to Judah, to the city where my ancestors are buried, so I can rebuild it.”",
        "The king, with the queen sitting beside him, asked me, “How long will your trip take, and when will you come back?” The king was glad to send me, and I gave him a date.",
        "I also told the king, “If it pleases the king, let me have letters for the governors on the other side of the river (the Euphrates), so they will let me pass through their lands until I reach Judah.”",
