        "Then some of the Levites stood up on the platform: Jeshua, Bani, Kadmiel, Shebaniah, Bunni, Sherebiah, Bani, and Chenani. They called out with loud voices to the Lord their God.",
        "Then the Levites Jeshua, Kadmiel, Bani, Hashabniah, Sherebiah, Hodijah, Shebaniah, and Pethahiah said, “Stand up and praise the Lord your God forever and ever. Blessed be Your glorious name, which is lifted high above all blessing and praise.”",
        "You alone are the Lord. You made the heavens, even the highest heavens, and all the stars and beings in them. You made the earth and everything on it, the seas and everything in them. You keep them all alive, and the armies of heaven bow down to You.",
        "You are the Lord, the God who chose Abram. You brought him out of Ur of the Chaldees and gave him the name Abraham.",
        "You found that his heart was faithful to You. You made a covenant with him to give his descendants the land of the Canaanites, the Hittites, the Amorites, the Perizzites, the Jebusites, and the Girgashites. And You kept Your word, because You are righteous.",
        "You saw how our ancestors suffered in Egypt, and You heard them cry out at the Red Sea.",
        "You did signs and miracles against Pharaoh, against all his officials, and against all the people of his land, because You knew how proudly they had treated our people. You made a name for Yourself that lasts to this day.",
        "You split the sea in front of them, and they walked through the middle of it on dry ground. But You threw the men chasing them into the deep water, like a stone sinking in mighty waves.",
        "You led them with a pillar of cloud in the daytime and a pillar of fire at night, to light up the road they were to travel.",
        "You came down on Mount Sinai and spoke with them from heaven. You gave them fair rules and true laws, good statutes and commandments.",
        "You taught them about Your holy Sabbath, and You gave them commandments, statutes, and laws through Your servant Moses.",
        "When they were hungry, You gave them bread from heaven. When they were thirsty, You brought water out of a rock for them. You told them to go in and take the land You had promised with an oath to give them.",
        "But our ancestors became proud and stubborn, and they did not obey Your commandments.",
        "They refused to listen. They forgot the miracles You had done for them. They became stubborn, and in their rebellion they chose a leader to take them back to slavery. But You are a God who forgives. You are kind and full of mercy, slow to get angry, and rich in faithful love. You did not abandon them.",
        "They even made themselves a calf out of melted metal and said, “This is your god who brought you up out of Egypt!” They did terrible things that insulted You.",
        "Yet because of Your great mercy, You did not abandon them in the wilderness. In the daytime the pillar of cloud never left them, but kept leading them on their way. At night the pillar of fire never left them, but kept lighting up the road they were to travel.",
        "You gave Your good Spirit to teach them. You did not hold back Your manna from their mouths, and You gave them water when they were thirsty.",
        "For forty years You took care of them in the wilderness, and they had everything they needed. Their clothes did not wear out, and their feet did not swell.",
        "You gave them kingdoms and nations, and You divided the land among them, down to its far corners. So they took over the land of Sihon, the land of the king of Heshbon, and the land of Og, the king of Bashan.",
        "You made their children as many as the stars in the sky. You brought them into the land You had told their ancestors they would go in and take.",
        "So their children went in and took the land. You beat down the Canaanites who lived there in front of them. You handed them over to Israel, with their kings and the people of the land, so Israel could do with them whatever they wanted.",
        "They captured walled cities and rich farmland. They took over houses full of good things, wells that were already dug, vineyards, olive groves, and plenty of fruit trees. So they ate until they were full and grew fat, and they enjoyed Your great goodness.",
        "But they disobeyed and rebelled against You. They threw Your law behind their backs. They killed Your prophets, who warned them to come back to You. They did terrible things that insulted You.",
        "So You handed them over to their enemies, who made them suffer. In their time of trouble they cried out to You, and You heard them from heaven. Because of Your great mercy You gave them rescuers, who saved them from their enemies.",
        "But as soon as they had peace, they did evil in Your sight again. So You left them in the hands of their enemies, who ruled over them. Yet when they turned back and cried out to You, You heard them from heaven. Many times You rescued them because of Your mercy.",
        "You warned them so You could bring them back to Your law. But they were proud and did not obey Your commandments. They sinned against Your laws, the very laws that give life to anyone who keeps them. They turned their backs on You. They were stubborn and would not listen.",
        "For many years You were patient with them. Your Spirit warned them through Your prophets, but they would not listen. So You handed them over to the nations around them.",
        "But because of Your great mercy You did not wipe them out or abandon them, because You are a kind and merciful God.",
        "So now, our God, the great, mighty, and awesome God, who keeps the covenant and faithful love: do not treat as small all the trouble that has come on us. It has come on our kings, our leaders, our priests, our prophets, our ancestors, and all Your people, from the days of the kings of Assyria until today.",
        "You have been fair in everything that has happened to us. You have been faithful, but we have done wrong.",
        "Our kings, our leaders, our priests, and our ancestors did not keep Your law. They did not pay attention to Your commandments or the warnings You gave them.",
        "Even while they had their own kingdom, with all the good things You gave them, and in the wide, rich land You set in front of them, they did not serve You or turn away from their evil ways.",
        "Look at us! Today we are servants. In the very land You gave our ancestors so they could eat its fruit and its good things, look, we are servants!",
        "Its large harvests go to the kings You have put over us because of our sins. They rule over our bodies and our cattle as they please, and we are in great trouble.",
        "Because of all this, we are making a firm agreement and writing it down. Our leaders, our Levites, and our priests are putting their seals on it."
