        "When Mordecai learned everything that had been done, he tore his clothes and put on sackcloth (rough cloth worn when mourning) and ashes. He went out into the middle of the city, crying out loudly and bitterly.",
        "He went only as far as the front of the king’s gate, because no one dressed in sackcloth was allowed to go through the king’s gate.",
        "In every province where the king’s order and law arrived, the Jews mourned greatly. They fasted, wept, and wailed, and many lay down on sackcloth and ashes.",
        "When Esther’s servant girls and her chamberlains (palace officers) came and told her, the queen was terribly upset. She sent clothes for Mordecai to wear so he could take off his sackcloth, but he would not take them.",
        "Then Esther called for Hatach, one of the king’s chamberlains whom the king had chosen to serve her. She sent him to Mordecai to find out what was wrong and why.",
        "So Hatach went out to Mordecai in the open square of the city in front of the king’s gate.",
        "Mordecai told him everything that had happened to him. He also told him the exact amount of money Haman had promised to pay into the king’s treasury to have the Jews destroyed.",
        "He also gave him a copy of the written law that had been announced in Shushan to destroy them. He told Hatach to show it to Esther, explain it to her, and tell her to go to the king to beg for his mercy and plead with him for her people.",
        "Hatach came back and told Esther what Mordecai had said.",
        "Then Esther spoke to Hatach and gave him this message for Mordecai:",
        "“All the king’s servants and the people of the king’s provinces know that any man or woman who goes to the king in the inner courtyard without being called has only one law: that person must be put to death. The only exception is if the king holds out his golden scepter (a royal rod) to them. Then they may live. But I have not been called to go in to the king for thirty days now.”",
        "So they told Mordecai what Esther had said.",
        "Then Mordecai sent back this answer to Esther: “Don’t think that just because you are in the king’s palace, you will escape any more than all the other Jews.”",
        "“If you stay silent at a time like this, help and rescue for the Jews will come from somewhere else, but you and your father’s family will be destroyed. And who knows? Maybe you have become queen for a time just like this.”",
        "Then Esther sent this answer back to Mordecai:",
        "“Go and gather all the Jews who are in Shushan, and fast for me. Don’t eat or drink for three days, night or day. My servant girls and I will fast the same way. Then I will go in to the king, even though it is against the law. And if I die, I die.”",
