        "The day came: the thirteenth day of the twelfth month, the month of Adar, when the king’s order and law were to be carried out. On that day the enemies of the Jews had hoped to overpower them. But things were turned around, and the Jews overpowered those who hated them.",
        "The Jews gathered in their cities in all the provinces of King Ahasuerus to attack those who wanted to harm them. No one could stand against them, because all the peoples had become afraid of them.",
        "All the officials of the provinces, the high officials, the governors, and the king’s officers helped the Jews, because they had become afraid of Mordecai.",
        "For Mordecai was a powerful man in the king’s palace, and news about him spread through all the provinces. This man Mordecai kept growing more and more powerful.",
        "So the Jews struck down all their enemies with the sword, killing and destroying them. They did whatever they wanted to those who hated them.",
        "In the fortress city of Shushan, the Jews killed and destroyed five hundred men.",
        "They also killed Parshandatha, Dalphon, Aspatha,",
        "Poratha, Adalia, Aridatha,",
        "Parmashta, Arisai, Aridai, and Vajezatha.",
        "These were the ten sons of Haman the son of Hammedatha, the enemy of the Jews. They killed them, but they did not take any of their belongings.",
        "That same day the number of people killed in the fortress city of Shushan was reported to the king.",
        "The king said to Queen Esther, “In the fortress city of Shushan the Jews have killed and destroyed five hundred men and the ten sons of Haman. What have they done in the rest of the king’s provinces? Now what do you want to ask? It will be given to you. What else do you want? It will be done.”",
        "Esther said, “If it pleases the king, let the Jews in Shushan be allowed to do the same tomorrow as today’s law allows. And let Haman’s ten sons be hanged on the pole.”",
        "So the king ordered it to be done. The law was announced in Shushan, and they hanged Haman’s ten sons.",
        "The Jews in Shushan gathered again on the fourteenth day of the month of Adar, and they killed three hundred men in Shushan. But they did not take any of their belongings.",
        "Meanwhile, the other Jews in the king’s provinces gathered and defended their lives. They got rest from their enemies and killed seventy-five thousand of those who hated them. But they did not take any of their belongings.",
        "This happened on the thirteenth day of the month of Adar. On the fourteenth day they rested and made it a day of feasting and joy.",
        "But the Jews in Shushan gathered on the thirteenth and the fourteenth days. So they rested on the fifteenth day and made it a day of feasting and joy.",
        "That is why the Jews in the country, who live in towns without walls, make the fourteenth day of the month of Adar a day of joy and feasting, a holiday, and a day for sending gifts of food to one another.",
        "Mordecai wrote down these events and sent letters to all the Jews in all the provinces of King Ahasuerus, both near and far.",
        "He told them to celebrate the fourteenth and fifteenth days of the month of Adar every year.",
        "These were the days when the Jews got rest from their enemies, and the month when their sorrow turned into joy and their mourning into a holiday. He told them to make these days of feasting and joy, of sending gifts of food to one another, and of giving gifts to the poor.",
        "So the Jews agreed to keep doing what they had started, as Mordecai had written to them.",
        "For Haman the son of Hammedatha the Agagite, the enemy of all the Jews, had made a plan against the Jews to destroy them. He had cast Pur, that is, the lot, to crush them and destroy them.",
        "But when Esther came before the king, he gave a written order that Haman’s evil plan against the Jews should come back on his own head, and that he and his sons should be hanged on the pole.",
        "That is why these days are called Purim, from the word Pur. So because of everything written in this letter, and because of what they had seen and what had happened to them,",
