        "These days were to be remembered and kept in every generation, by every family, in every province, and in every city. These days of Purim were never to stop being kept among the Jews, and the memory of them was never to die out among their children.",
        "Then Queen Esther, the daughter of Abihail, and Mordecai the Jew wrote with full authority to confirm this second letter about Purim.",
