        "While all this was going on, I was not in Jerusalem. In the thirty-second year that Artaxerxes was king of Babylon, I had gone back to the king. After some time I asked the king to let me leave,",
        "and I came back to Jerusalem. Then I found out about the evil thing Eliashib had done for Tobiah by giving him a room in the courtyards of the house of God.",
        "It made me very upset, so I threw all of Tobiah’s belongings out of the room.",
        "Then I gave orders, and they made the rooms clean and pure again. I put the dishes and tools of the house of God back in them, along with the grain offerings and the frankincense.",
        "I also found out that the Levites had not been given their share. So the Levites and singers who did the work had all run off, each one to his own field.",
        "So I scolded the officials and said, “Why has the house of God been neglected?” Then I called the Levites and singers back together and put them back at their posts.",
        "Then all the people of Judah brought the tithe of their grain, new wine, and olive oil to the storerooms.",
        "I put men in charge of the storerooms: Shelemiah the priest, Zadok the scribe, and a Levite named Pedaiah. Hanan son of Zaccur, the son of Mattaniah, was their helper. These men were known to be honest, and their job was to hand out the supplies to their fellow workers.",
        "My God, remember me for this. Do not erase the good things I have faithfully done for the house of my God and for its services.",
        "In those days I saw people in Judah stomping grapes in winepresses on the Sabbath. I saw them bringing in bundles of grain and loading them on donkeys. They were also bringing wine, grapes, figs, and all kinds of loads into Jerusalem on the Sabbath day. So I warned them on the day they sold food.",
        "Men from Tyre were living in Jerusalem too. They brought in fish and all kinds of goods and sold them on the Sabbath to the people of Judah, right there in Jerusalem.",
        "So I scolded the important men of Judah. I said to them, “What is this evil thing you are doing? You are treating the Sabbath day as if it were not holy!”",
        "“Isn’t this just what your ancestors did? And didn’t our God bring all this trouble on us and on this city because of it? Now you are making God even angrier with Israel by not keeping the Sabbath holy!”",
        "So when the gates of Jerusalem began to get dark before the Sabbath, I ordered the doors to be shut. I said they must not be opened until the Sabbath was over. I put some of my own servants at the gates so that no loads could be brought in on the Sabbath day.",
        "Once or twice the traders and the sellers of all kinds of goods spent the night outside Jerusalem.",
