        "Make him drunk, because he lifted himself up proudly against the Lord. Moab will roll around in his own vomit, and people will laugh at him too.",
        "Wasn’t Israel the one you laughed at, Moab? Was he caught among thieves? Every time you talked about him, you shook your head at him in scorn.",
        "You people living in Moab, leave the cities and go live among the rocks. Be like a dove that builds its nest in the sides of a cliff opening.",
        "We have heard about Moab’s pride. He is very proud. We have heard of his conceit, his arrogance, his pride, and how high and mighty his heart is.",
        "I know how angry and insolent he is, says the Lord, but it will come to nothing. His boasting will not get anything done.",
        "So I will wail for Moab. I will cry out for all of Moab. I will mourn for the men of Kir-heres.",
        "Vine of Sibmah, I will weep for you as Jazer weeps. Your branches spread across the sea and reached as far as the sea of Jazer. The destroyer has attacked your summer fruit and your grape harvest.",
        "Joy and gladness are gone from the rich farmland and from the land of Moab. I have stopped the wine from flowing from the winepresses. No one stomps the grapes with happy shouts. The shouting they hear is not shouting for joy.",
        "Cries go up from Heshbon all the way to Elealeh and Jahaz. They are heard from Zoar to Horonaim, like a three-year-old young cow. Even the waters of Nimrim have dried up.",
        "In Moab, says the Lord, I will put an end to those who offer sacrifices at the high places (hilltop shrines) and burn incense to their gods.",
        "So My heart moans for Moab like a mournful flute. My heart moans like a flute for the men of Kir-heres, because the wealth they gained is lost.",
        "Every head is shaved and every beard is cut off. Every hand has cuts on it, and everyone wears sackcloth (rough cloth worn when mourning) around the waist.",
        "On all the rooftops of Moab and in its streets, everyone is mourning. For I have broken Moab like a jar nobody wants, says the Lord.",
        "They will wail, “How it is broken! How Moab has turned his back in shame!” Moab will be laughed at, and everyone around him will look at him in horror.",
        "For this is what the Lord says: Look! He will swoop down like an eagle and spread his wings over Moab.",
        "Kerioth is captured, and the fortresses are taken. On that day the hearts of Moab’s warriors will be like the heart of a woman in labor pains.",
        "Moab will be destroyed and no longer be a nation, because he lifted himself up proudly against the Lord.",
        "Terror, the pit, and the trap are waiting for you, you who live in Moab, says the Lord.",
        "Whoever runs from the terror will fall into the pit. Whoever climbs out of the pit will be caught in the trap. For I will bring on Moab the year of their punishment, says the Lord.",
        "Those who ran away stood in the shadow of Heshbon, with no strength left. But a fire has come out of Heshbon, a flame from the middle of Sihon’s land. It burns up the edges of Moab and the heads of the loud, boastful people.",
        "Woe to you, Moab! The people of Chemosh are destroyed. Your sons have been taken captive, and your daughters have been taken into exile.",
        "Yet in the last days I will bring the captives of Moab back, says the Lord. This is the end of the judgment on Moab."
