        "Say: What was your mother? A lioness! She lay down among the lions. She raised her cubs among the young lions.",
        "She raised one of her cubs, and he grew into a strong young lion. He learned to hunt and tear his prey, and he ate people.",
        "The nations heard about him. He was caught in their pit, and they dragged him with hooks to the land of Egypt.",
        "When she saw that she had waited for nothing and her hope was gone, she took another one of her cubs and made him a strong young lion.",
        "He prowled among the lions and grew into a strong young lion. He learned to hunt and tear his prey, and he ate people.",
        "He came to know their palaces and left them in ruins, and he laid waste their cities. The land and everything in it was terrified by the sound of his roaring.",
        "Then the nations from the lands all around came against him. They spread their net over him, and he was caught in their pit.",
        "They put him in a cage with hooks and brought him to the king of Babylon. They locked him up in a fortress, so his roar would never be heard again on the mountains of Israel.",
        "Your mother was like a vine in your blood, planted by the water. She had plenty of fruit and was full of branches because there was so much water.",
        "She had strong branches, good enough to be the scepters of rulers. She grew tall above the thick branches and she stood out because she was so tall and had so many branches.",
        "But she was pulled up by the roots in anger and thrown to the ground. The east wind dried up her fruit. Her strong branches were broken off and dried up, and fire burned them up.",
        "Now she is planted in the wilderness, in a dry land with no water.",
        "Fire has spread from one of her branches and burned up her fruit. No strong branch is left on her to be a ruler’s scepter. This is a song of mourning, and it will be sung as a song of mourning."
