        "This was in the first year of Darius the son of Ahasuerus, a Mede by birth, who was made king over the kingdom of the Chaldeans.",
        "In the first year of his rule, I, Daniel, learned from the books how many years Jerusalem would lie in ruins. The word of the Lord had told Jeremiah the prophet that it would be seventy years.",
        "So I turned to the Lord God and pleaded with Him in prayer. I fasted, wore sackcloth, and sat in ashes.",
        "I prayed to the Lord my God and confessed. I said, “O Lord, the great and awesome God, You keep the covenant and show mercy to those who love Him and keep His commandments.”",
        "We have sinned and done wrong. We have been wicked and have rebelled. We have turned away from Your commandments and Your laws.",
        "We have not listened to Your servants the prophets, who spoke in Your name to our kings, our leaders, our fathers, and all the people of the land.",
        "Lord, You are always in the right, but we are covered with shame, as we are today: the men of Judah, the people living in Jerusalem, and all Israel, near and far, in all the countries where You have driven them because they were unfaithful to You.",
        "Lord, we are covered with shame, our kings, our leaders, and our fathers, because we have sinned against You.",
        "But the Lord our God is merciful and forgiving, even though we have rebelled against Him.",
        "We have not obeyed the voice of the Lord our God or lived by His laws, which He gave us through His servants the prophets.",
        "All Israel has broken Your law and turned away, refusing to obey Your voice. So the curse has been poured out on us, the oath written in the law of Moses, the servant of God, because we have sinned against Him.",
        "He has done what He said He would do to us and to the rulers who ruled us. He has brought a terrible disaster on us. Nothing under the whole sky has ever been done like what was done to Jerusalem.",
        "All this disaster has come on us, just as the law of Moses says. Yet we have not prayed to the Lord our God for His favor by turning away from our sins and paying attention to Your truth.",
        "So the Lord kept the disaster ready and brought it on us. The Lord our God is right in everything He does, but we did not obey His voice.",
        "And now, Lord our God, You brought Your people out of the land of Egypt with Your mighty power and made a name for Yourself that lasts to this day. We have sinned. We have been wicked.",
        "Lord, because You always do what is right, please turn Your anger and fury away from Your city Jerusalem, Your holy mountain. Because of our sins and the sins of our fathers, Jerusalem and Your people have become a disgrace to everyone around us.",
        "So now, our God, hear the prayer of Your servant and his pleading. For Your own sake, Lord, let Your face shine on Your sanctuary that lies in ruins.",
        "My God, turn Your ear and listen. Open Your eyes and see our ruins and the city that is called by Your name. We are not pleading with You because we are good, but because You are so merciful.",
        "Lord, listen! Lord, forgive! Lord, hear us and act! For Your own sake, my God, do not wait, because Your city and Your people are called by Your name.",
        "I was still speaking and praying, confessing my sin and the sin of my people Israel, and pleading with the Lord my God for His holy mountain.",
        "While I was still praying, Gabriel, the man I had seen in the earlier vision, came flying swiftly and touched me about the time of the evening offering.",
        "He explained things to me and talked with me. He said, “Daniel, I have come now to give you insight and understanding.”",
        "As soon as you began to pray, a command went out, and I have come to tell it to you, because you are greatly loved. So think about the message and understand the vision.",
        "Seventy weeks (seventy sets of seven) have been decided for your people and your holy city. They are to finish the rebellion, put an end to sins, make atonement for wickedness, bring in righteousness that lasts forever, seal up vision and prophecy, and anoint the Most Holy.",
        "Know this and understand it: from the time the command goes out to restore and rebuild Jerusalem until the Messiah, the Prince, comes, there will be seven weeks and sixty-two weeks. The street and the wall will be built again, but in hard times.",
        "After the sixty-two weeks, the Messiah will be cut off, but not for himself. The people of the prince who is coming will destroy the city and the sanctuary. Its end will come like a flood, and ruin has been decided until the end of the war.",
        "He will make a firm covenant with many for one week. In the middle of the week he will put a stop to the sacrifice and the offering. Because of the spreading of disgusting things, he will make it desolate, until the full end that has been decided is poured out on the desolate."
