        "On the twenty-fourth day of the first month, I was standing on the bank of the great river Hiddekel (the Tigris).",
        "I looked up and saw a man dressed in linen, with a belt of fine gold from Uphaz around his waist.",
        "His body was like beryl (a shining gemstone). His face looked like lightning, his eyes were like burning torches, and his arms and feet gleamed like polished bronze. His voice sounded like the roar of a huge crowd.",
        "Only I, Daniel, saw the vision. The men who were with me did not see it, but they were struck with terror and ran away to hide.",
        "So I was left alone, looking at this great vision. All my strength drained out of me. My face turned deathly pale, and I had no strength left.",
        "Then I heard the sound of his words. As I listened, I fell into a deep sleep, lying with my face to the ground.",
        "Suddenly a hand touched me and lifted me, shaking, onto my hands and knees.",
