        "And I myself, in the first year of Darius the Mede, stood up to support him and give him strength.",
        "Now I will tell you the truth. Three more kings will rise up in Persia. Then a fourth king will be far richer than all of them. When he has grown strong through his riches, he will stir up everyone against the kingdom of Grecia (Greece).",
        "Then a mighty king will rise up. He will rule with great power and do whatever he wants.",
        "But as soon as he has risen, his kingdom will be broken apart and split up toward the four winds of heaven. It will not go to his descendants, and it will not have the power he ruled with. His kingdom will be pulled up by the roots and given to others besides them.",
        "The king of the south will become strong. But one of his commanders will grow stronger than he is and will rule, and his kingdom will be a great one.",
        "After some years they will join together. The daughter of the king of the south will come to the king of the north to make a peace agreement. But she will not keep her power, and he will not last, and neither will his strength. She will be handed over, along with the people who brought her, her father, and the one who supported her in those times.",
