        "When he has carried off that army, his heart will swell with pride. He will strike down tens of thousands, but he will not stay strong because of it.",
        "For the king of the north will come back and raise an army bigger than the first one. After some years he will surely come with a great army and many supplies.",
        "In those times many people will rise up against the king of the south. Violent men from your own people will also lift themselves up to make the vision come true, but they will fall.",
        "Then the king of the north will come, build a siege ramp, and capture a strongly walled city. The forces of the south will not be able to stand against him, not even their best troops. They will have no strength left to hold out.",
        "The one who comes against him will do whatever he wants, and no one will be able to stand up to him. He will take his stand in the glorious land (Israel), and his hand will bring it to ruin.",
        "He will also make up his mind to come with the strength of his whole kingdom, bringing upright men with him. Here is what he will do: he will give him a young woman as a wife, to corrupt her. But she will not stand on his side or be for him.",
        "After this he will turn his attention to the islands and coastlands and capture many of them. But a commander, acting for himself, will put an end to his insults. Without suffering any shame himself, he will turn those insults back on him.",
        "Then he will turn back toward the fortresses of his own land. But he will stumble and fall, and he will be seen no more.",
        "Someone will rise up in his place who sends out a tax collector through the glorious kingdom. But within a few days he will be destroyed, though not in anger and not in battle.",
        "In his place a contemptible man will rise up, someone people never gave the honor of being king. But he will come in quietly, while people feel safe, and take the kingdom by smooth talk and trickery.",
        "Whole armies will be swept away before him like a flood and broken. The prince of the covenant will be broken too.",
        "After an agreement is made with him, he will act with deceit. He will rise up and become powerful with only a small group of people.",
        "He will come in peacefully, even into the richest places of the province. He will do what his fathers and his fathers’ fathers never did. He will hand out plunder, loot, and riches among them. He will make plans against the strongholds, but only for a time.",
        "With a great army he will stir up his power and his courage against the king of the south. The king of the south will get ready for battle with a very great and mighty army. But he will not stand, because people will make plots against him.",
        "The very people who eat the food from his table will destroy him. His army will be swept away as if by a flood, and many will fall dead.",
        "Both of these kings will have their hearts set on doing evil. They will sit at the same table and tell each other lies, but it will not succeed, because the end will still come at the time that has been set.",
        "Then the king of the north will go back to his land with great riches. But his heart will be against the holy covenant. He will carry out his plans and then return to his own land.",
        "At the appointed time he will come back and march toward the south. But this time it will not turn out like the first time or the time after.",
