        "The Passover and the Feast of Unleavened Bread were two days away. The chief priests and the scribes were looking for a sly way to arrest Him and put Him to death.",
        "But they said, “Not during the feast, or the people may riot.”",
        "Jesus was in Bethany, at the house of Simon the leper. As He sat at the table, a woman came with an alabaster jar (a jar carved from soft white stone) of very expensive perfume made of spikenard. She broke the jar and poured the perfume on His head.",
        "Some of the people there were angry and said to each other, “Why was this perfume wasted?”",
        "“It could have been sold for more than three hundred pence (about a year’s pay) and the money given to the poor.” And they grumbled at her.",
        "But Jesus said, “Leave her alone. Why are you bothering her? She has done a good thing for Me.”",
        "“You will always have the poor with you, and you can do good for them whenever you want. But you will not always have Me.”",
        "“She has done what she could. She came ahead of time to anoint My body for its burial.”",
        "“I tell you the truth: wherever this gospel is preached in the whole world, what she has done will also be told in memory of her.”",
        "Then Judas Iscariot, one of the twelve, went to the chief priests to hand Jesus over to them.",
        "When they heard it, they were glad and promised to give him money. So he looked for a good chance to betray Him.",
        "On the first day of the Feast of Unleavened Bread, when the Passover lamb was killed, His disciples asked Him, “Where do You want us to go and get things ready for You to eat the Passover?”",
        "So He sent two of His disciples and told them, “Go into the city, and a man carrying a jar of water will meet you. Follow him.”",
        "“Whatever house he goes into, tell the owner, ‘The Teacher asks, where is the guest room where I can eat the Passover with My disciples?’”",
        "“He will show you a large upstairs room, furnished and ready. Get things ready for us there.”",
        "His disciples left and went into the city. They found everything just as He had told them, and they prepared the Passover.",
        "When evening came, He arrived with the twelve.",
        "As they sat eating, Jesus said, “I tell you the truth, one of you who is eating with Me will betray Me.”",
        "They became very sad and began to ask Him, one by one, “Is it me?” And another asked, “Is it me?”",
        "He answered them, “It is one of the twelve, the one who is dipping into the dish with Me.”",
        "“The Son of Man is going, just as it is written about Him. But woe (great sorrow is coming) to the man who betrays the Son of Man! It would have been better for that man if he had never been born.”",
        "While they were eating, Jesus took bread, blessed it, broke it, and gave it to them. He said, “Take it and eat. This is My body.”",
        "Then He took the cup, and after He gave thanks, He gave it to them, and they all drank from it.",
        "He said to them, “This is My blood of the new covenant, which is poured out for many.”",
        "“I tell you the truth, I will not drink the fruit of the vine again until the day I drink it new in the kingdom of God.”",
        "After they sang a hymn, they went out to the Mount of Olives.",
        "Jesus said to them, “All of you will stumble and fall away because of Me tonight. For it is written, ‘I will strike the shepherd, and the sheep will be scattered.’”",
        "“But after I have risen, I will go ahead of you into Galilee.”",
        "Peter said to Him, “Even if everyone else falls away, I will not.”",
        "Jesus said to him, “I tell you the truth: today, this very night, before the rooster crows twice, you will deny Me three times.”",
        "But Peter insisted even more strongly, “Even if I have to die with You, I will never deny You!” And all the others said the same thing.",
        "They came to a place called Gethsemane, and He said to His disciples, “Sit here while I pray.”",
        "He took Peter and James and John with Him, and He began to be deeply troubled and weighed down with distress.",
        "He said to them, “My soul is full of sorrow, even to the point of death. Stay here and keep watch.”",
        "He went a little farther, fell to the ground, and prayed that, if it were possible, the hour might pass from Him.",
        "He said, “Abba (Aramaic for Father), Father, all things are possible for You. Take this cup away from Me. Yet not what I want, but what You want.”",
        "Then He came back and found them sleeping. He said to Peter, “Simon, are you asleep? Couldn’t you stay awake and keep watch for one hour?”",
        "“Keep watch and pray so that you will not fall into temptation. The spirit really is willing, but the flesh is weak.”",
        "He went away again and prayed, saying the same words.",
        "When He came back, He found them asleep again, because their eyes were heavy. They did not know what to say to Him.",
        "He came a third time and said to them, “Go on sleeping now and rest. It is enough. The hour has come. Look, the Son of Man is being handed over to sinners.”",
        "“Get up, let’s go. Look, the one who is betraying Me is near.”",
        "Right then, while He was still speaking, Judas, one of the twelve, came. With him was a large crowd carrying swords and clubs, sent from the chief priests, the scribes, and the elders.",
        "The betrayer had given them a signal: “The One I kiss is the man. Seize Him and lead Him away under guard.”",
        "As soon as he arrived, he went straight to Jesus and said, “Rabbi, Rabbi!” and kissed Him.",
        "Then they grabbed Him and arrested Him.",
        "One of those standing nearby pulled out a sword and struck the high priest’s servant, cutting off his ear.",
        "Jesus said to them, “Have you come out with swords and clubs to capture Me, as if I were a robber?”",
        "“Every day I was with you in the temple, teaching, and you did not arrest Me. But the scriptures must be fulfilled.”",
        "Then they all left Him and ran away.",
        "A certain young man was following Him, with only a linen cloth wrapped around his bare body. The young men grabbed him,",
        "but he left the linen cloth behind and ran away from them naked.",
        "They led Jesus away to the high priest. All the chief priests, the elders, and the scribes gathered there with him.",
        "Peter followed Him from a distance, right into the courtyard of the high priest. He sat with the guards and warmed himself at the fire.",
        "The chief priests and the whole council were looking for testimony against Jesus so they could put Him to death, but they found none.",
        "Many told lies about Him in court, but their stories did not agree.",
        "Then some men stood up and told lies about Him, saying,",
        "“We heard Him say, ‘I will destroy this temple made with hands, and in three days I will build another one not made with hands.’”",
        "But even then their stories did not agree.",
        "Then the high priest stood up in front of everyone and asked Jesus, “Aren’t You going to answer? What about these things these men are saying against You?”",
        "But He stayed silent and gave no answer. Again the high priest asked Him, “Are You the Christ, the Son of the Blessed One?”",
        "Jesus said, “I am. And you will see the Son of Man sitting at the right hand of power and coming in the clouds of heaven.”",
        "Then the high priest tore his clothes and said, “Why do we need any more witnesses?”",
        "“You have heard the blasphemy (His insult against God). What do you think?” And they all condemned Him as deserving death.",
        "Then some began to spit on Him. They covered His face, hit Him with their fists, and said to Him, “Prophesy!” And the guards slapped Him with their open hands.",
        "While Peter was below in the courtyard, one of the high priest’s servant girls came by.",
        "When she saw Peter warming himself, she looked closely at him and said, “You were with Jesus of Nazareth too.”",
        "But he denied it and said, “I don’t know or understand what you are talking about.” Then he went out to the entryway, and the rooster crowed.",
        "The servant girl saw him again and began to say to those standing nearby, “This man is one of them.”",
        "But he denied it again. A little later, those standing nearby said to Peter again, “You really are one of them. You are a Galilæan, and the way you talk shows it.”",
        "But he began to call down curses on himself and to swear, “I don’t know this man you are talking about!”",
        "Then the rooster crowed a second time. Peter remembered what Jesus had said to him: “Before the rooster crows twice, you will deny Me three times.” And when he thought about it, he wept."
