        "Meanwhile His disciples kept urging Him, “Rabbi, eat something.”",
        "But He said to them, “I have food to eat that you don’t know about.”",
        "So the disciples asked each other, “Did someone bring Him something to eat?”",
        "Jesus said to them, “My food is to do the will of Him who sent Me, and to finish His work.”",
        "Don’t you say, ‘Four more months, and then the harvest comes’? Listen, I tell you, open your eyes and look at the fields. They are already white and ready to harvest.",
        "The one who harvests is being paid and is gathering a crop for eternal life, so that the one who plants and the one who harvests can be glad together.",
        "This shows the saying is true: ‘One person plants, and another harvests.’",
        "I sent you to harvest what you did not work for. Others did the hard work, and you have stepped in to gain from their work.",
        "Many of the Samaritans from that town believed in Him because the woman had testified, “He told me everything I ever did.”",
        "So when the Samaritans came to Him, they begged Him to stay with them, and He stayed there two days.",
        "And many more believed because of what He Himself said.",
