        "One day He was teaching, and Pharisees and teachers of the law were sitting nearby. They had come from every town in Galilee and Judæa, and from Jerusalem. And the power of the Lord was there to heal them.",
        "Just then some men came carrying a paralyzed man on a bed. They tried to bring him inside and lay him in front of Jesus.",
        "But the crowd was so big that they could not find a way to bring him in. So they climbed up on the roof and lowered him on his mat through the roof tiles, right into the middle of the crowd in front of Jesus.",
        "When Jesus saw their faith, He said to the man, “Friend, your sins are forgiven.”",
        "The scribes and the Pharisees began to think to themselves, “Who is this man who speaks against God? Who can forgive sins except God alone?”",
        "Jesus knew what they were thinking. He answered them, “Why are you thinking these things in your hearts?”",
        "“Which is easier: to say, ‘Your sins are forgiven,’ or to say, ‘Get up and walk’?”",
        "“But I want you to know that the Son of Man has authority on earth to forgive sins.” So He said to the paralyzed man, “I tell you, get up, pick up your mat, and go home.”",
        "Right away the man stood up in front of them, picked up the mat he had been lying on, and went home praising God.",
        "Everyone was amazed and praised God. They were filled with awe and said, “We have seen amazing things today.”",
        "After this, Jesus went out and saw a tax collector named Levi sitting at the booth where taxes were paid. He said to him, “Follow Me.”",
        "Levi got up, left everything, and followed Him.",
        "Then Levi held a big feast for Jesus at his house. A large crowd of tax collectors and other people were eating with them.",
        "But the scribes and Pharisees among them complained to His disciples, “Why do you eat and drink with tax collectors and sinners?”",
        "Jesus answered them, “Healthy people don’t need a doctor. Sick people do.”",
        "“I did not come to call righteous people to repent, but sinners.”",
        "They said to Him, “Why do John’s disciples often fast and pray, and the Pharisees’ disciples too, but Your disciples eat and drink?”",
        "Jesus said to them, “Can you make the wedding guests go without food while the bridegroom is still with them?”",
        "“But the time will come when the bridegroom will be taken away from them. Then, in those days, they will fast.”",
        "He also told them a parable: “No one sews a piece of a new garment onto an old one. If he does, the new one gets torn, and the patch from the new one does not match the old.”",
        "“And no one pours new wine into old wineskins (leather bags). If he does, the new wine will burst the skins, the wine will spill out, and the skins will be ruined.”",
        "“No, new wine has to be poured into new wineskins, and then both are kept safe.”",
        "“And no one who has been drinking old wine wants the new right away, because he says, ‘The old is better.’”"
