        "When that day comes, be glad and jump for joy, because you have a great reward in heaven. Their fathers treated the prophets the same way.",
        "But woe (great sorrow is coming) to you who are rich, because you have already received your comfort.",
        "Woe to you who are full, because you will go hungry. Woe to you who laugh now, because you will mourn and cry.",
        "Woe to you when everyone speaks well of you, because that is how their fathers treated the false prophets.",
        "But I tell you who are listening: Love your enemies. Do good to people who hate you.",
        "Bless those who curse you, and pray for those who treat you cruelly.",
        "If someone hits you on one cheek, offer him the other one too. If someone takes your cloak, don’t stop him from taking your coat too.",
        "Give to everyone who asks you for something. If someone takes away what belongs to you, don’t ask for it back.",
        "Treat other people the way you want them to treat you.",
        "If you love those who love you, why should anyone thank you for that? Even sinners love the people who love them.",
        "And if you do good to those who do good to you, why should anyone thank you for that? Even sinners do the same.",
        "And if you lend to people you expect to pay you back, why should anyone thank you for that? Even sinners lend to sinners so they can get back the same amount.",
        "Instead, love your enemies, do good, and lend without expecting anything back. Then your reward will be great, and you will be children of the Most High, because He is kind to people who are ungrateful and evil.",
        "So be merciful, just as your Father is merciful.",
        "Don’t judge others, and you will not be judged. Don’t condemn others, and you will not be condemned. Forgive, and you will be forgiven.",
        "Give, and it will be given to you. People will pour into your lap a full measure, pressed down, shaken together, and spilling over. The measure you use for others is the measure that will be used for you.",
        "He also told them a parable: “Can a blind person lead another blind person? Won’t they both fall into a ditch?”",
