        "Then He told them a parable: “A certain rich man’s land produced huge crops.”",
        "“He thought to himself, ‘What should I do? I don’t have anywhere to store my crops.’”",
        "“Then he said, ‘This is what I will do. I will tear down my barns and build bigger ones, and there I will store all my crops and my goods.’”",
        "“‘And I will say to my soul: Soul, you have plenty of good things stored up for many years. Take it easy. Eat, drink, and enjoy yourself.’”",
        "“But God said to him, ‘You fool! This very night your soul will be demanded from you. Then who will get all the things you have gotten ready?’”",
        "“That is how it is for anyone who stores up treasure for himself but is not rich toward God.”",
        "Then He said to His disciples, “So I tell you, don’t worry about your life, about what you will eat, or about your body, about what you will wear.”",
        "“Life is more than food, and the body is more than clothes.”",
        "“Think about the ravens. They don’t plant or harvest, and they have no storeroom or barn, yet God feeds them. You are worth so much more than birds!”",
