        "A large crowd was gathering, and people were coming to Him from every town. So He told them a parable:",
        "A farmer went out to plant his seed. As he scattered it, some seed fell along the path. People stepped on it, and the birds of the air ate it up.",
        "Some fell on rock. As soon as it came up, it dried up, because it had no moisture.",
        "Some fell among thorns. The thorns grew up with it and choked it.",
        "Other seed fell on good soil. It grew and produced a hundred times as much as was planted. When He had said this, He called out, “Whoever has ears to hear should listen.”",
        "His disciples asked Him, “What does this parable mean?”",
