        "(Jesus had commanded the unclean spirit to come out of the man. Many times it had taken hold of him. Even when he was kept bound with chains and leg irons, he broke the chains, and the demon drove him out into the wilderness.)",
        "Jesus asked him, “What is your name?” He answered, “Legion” (a Roman army unit of thousands of soldiers), because many demons had gone into him.",
        "The demons kept begging Jesus not to order them to go into the abyss (the bottomless pit).",
        "A large herd of pigs was feeding there on the hillside. The demons begged Jesus to let them go into the pigs, and He let them.",
        "Then the demons came out of the man and went into the pigs. The herd rushed down the steep bank into the lake and drowned.",
        "When the men taking care of the pigs saw what had happened, they ran away and told the news in the city and the countryside.",
        "So people went out to see what had happened. They came to Jesus and found the man the demons had left. He was sitting at Jesus’ feet, dressed and thinking clearly. And they were afraid.",
        "The people who had seen it told them how the man who had been possessed by demons was healed.",
        "Then all the people from the area around the Gadarenes asked Jesus to go away from them, because they were very frightened. So He got into the boat and went back.",
        "The man the demons had left begged to go with Jesus. But Jesus sent him away and said,",
        "“Go back home and tell what great things God has done for you.” So the man went and told people all over the city what great things Jesus had done for him.",
        "When Jesus came back, the crowd welcomed Him gladly, because they had all been waiting for Him.",
        "Just then a man named Jairus came. He was a leader of the synagogue. He fell down at Jesus’ feet and begged Him to come to his house,",
        "because his only daughter, who was about twelve years old, was dying. As Jesus went, the crowds pressed in around Him.",
        "A woman was there who had been bleeding for twelve years. She had spent everything she had on doctors, but no one could heal her.",
        "She came up behind Him and touched the edge of His robe. Right away her bleeding stopped.",
        "Jesus asked, “Who touched Me?” Everyone said they hadn’t. Peter and those with him said, “Master, the crowds are pushing and pressing against You, and You ask who touched You?”",
        "But Jesus said, “Someone touched Me. I know that power has gone out from Me.”",
        "When the woman saw that she could not stay hidden, she came trembling and fell down in front of Him. In front of all the people, she told Him why she had touched Him and how she had been healed right away.",
