        "“They will say, ‘This man started to build, but he couldn’t finish.’”",
        "“Or suppose a king is going out to fight a war against another king. Won’t he first sit down and think it over? Can he and his ten thousand soldiers face the king who is coming against him with twenty thousand?”",
        "“If not, while the other king is still far away, he will send messengers to ask for terms of peace.”",
        "“In the same way, any one of you who does not give up everything he has cannot be My disciple.”",
        "“Salt is good. But if the salt loses its taste, how can it be made salty again?”",
