        "All who are led by the Spirit of God are God’s sons.",
        "You didn’t receive a spirit that makes you slaves and afraid all over again. You received the Spirit of adoption, and by Him we cry out, “Abba, Father!”",
        "The Spirit Himself testifies along with our own spirit that we are God’s children.",
        "And if we are children, then we are heirs: heirs of God, and heirs together with Christ, if we suffer with Him so that we will also be glorified with Him.",
        "I’m sure that what we suffer now isn’t worth comparing with the glory that will be shown in us.",
        "All of creation is eagerly waiting for the day when God’s sons will be revealed.",
        "Creation was made subject to emptiness, not by its own choice, but because of the One who made it that way, in hope",
        "that creation itself will also be set free from being a slave to decay and brought into the glorious freedom of God’s children.",
        "We know that the whole creation has been groaning together in pain, like a woman giving birth, right up to now.",
        "And not only creation, but we ourselves too, who have the first fruits of the Spirit, groan inside as we wait for our adoption, which is the redemption of our bodies.",
        "We were saved in hope. But hope that you can see isn’t hope. Why would anyone still hope for something he already sees?",
        "But if we hope for something we don’t see yet, then we wait for it patiently.",
