        "Paul looked straight at the council and said, “Brothers, I have lived before God with a completely good conscience, right up to this day.”",
        "Then the high priest Ananias ordered the men standing near Paul to hit him on the mouth.",
        "Then Paul said to him, “God will strike you, you whitewashed wall! You sit there to judge me by the law, and yet you break the law by ordering them to hit me?”",
        "The men standing nearby said, “How dare you insult God’s high priest?”",
        "Paul said, “Brothers, I did not know that he was the high priest. For it is written, ‘Do not speak evil about the ruler of your people.’”",
        "Then Paul, knowing that some of them were Sadducees and the others were Pharisees, called out in the council, “Brothers, I am a Pharisee, the son of a Pharisee. I am on trial because of the hope of the resurrection of the dead.”",
        "When he said this, an argument broke out between the Pharisees and the Sadducees, and the crowd split into two sides.",
        "For the Sadducees say there is no resurrection, and no angels or spirits, but the Pharisees believe in all of these.",
        "There was a great uproar. The scribes who belonged to the Pharisees’ group stood up and argued hard, saying, “We find nothing wrong with this man. But if a spirit or an angel has spoken to him, let us not fight against God.”",
        "The argument grew so violent that the commander was afraid they would tear Paul to pieces. He ordered the soldiers to go down, take him away from them by force, and bring him into the fortress.",
        "The next night the Lord stood beside Paul and said, “Take courage, Paul! Just as you have testified about Me in Jerusalem, you must also testify in Rome.”",
        "When morning came, some of the Jews made a plot together. They put themselves under a curse, swearing that they would not eat or drink until they had killed Paul.",
        "More than forty men were part of this plot.",
        "They went to the chief priests and elders and said, “We have put ourselves under a solemn curse not to eat anything until we have killed Paul.”",
        "“So now, you and the council ask the commander to bring him down to you tomorrow, as if you wanted to look into his case more carefully. We are ready to kill him before he gets here.”",
        "But the son of Paul’s sister heard about the ambush. So he went into the fortress and told Paul.",
        "Then Paul called one of the centurions (Roman officers over a hundred soldiers) and said, “Take this young man to the commander. He has something to tell him.”",
        "So the centurion took him to the commander and said, “Paul the prisoner called me over and asked me to bring this young man to you. He has something to tell you.”",
        "The commander took the young man by the hand, led him off by themselves, and asked, “What do you have to tell me?”",
        "He said, “The Jews have agreed to ask you to bring Paul down to the council tomorrow, as if they wanted to question him more carefully.”",
        "“But don’t let them talk you into it. More than forty of their men are hiding, waiting to attack him. They have sworn an oath not to eat or drink until they have killed him. They are ready now, just waiting for you to say yes.”",
        "So the commander sent the young man away and warned him, “Don’t tell anyone that you have told me about this.”",
        "Then he called two centurions and said, “Get two hundred soldiers ready to go to Cæsarea, along with seventy horsemen and two hundred spearmen. Leave at the third hour of the night (about nine o’clock tonight).”",
        "“Also provide animals for Paul to ride, and bring him safely to Felix the governor.”",
        "And he wrote a letter that said this:",
        "Claudius Lysias, to the most excellent Governor Felix: Greetings.",
        "This man was seized by the Jews, and they were about to kill him. Then I came with my troops and rescued him, because I had learned that he was a Roman citizen.",
        "I wanted to know why they were accusing him, so I brought him before their council.",
        "I found that he was accused over questions about their own law, but he was not charged with anything that deserved death or prison.",
        "When I was told that the Jews were planning to ambush the man, I sent him to you right away. I also ordered his accusers to tell you what they have against him. Farewell.",
        "So the soldiers did as they were ordered. They took Paul and brought him during the night to Antipatris.",
        "The next day they let the horsemen go on with him, and they went back to the fortress.",
        "When the horsemen came to Cæsarea, they gave the letter to the governor and also brought Paul before him.",
        "The governor read the letter and asked what province Paul was from. When he learned that he was from Cilicia,",
        "he said, “I will hear your case when your accusers also arrive.” And he ordered that Paul be kept under guard in Herod’s judgment hall (his palace headquarters)."
