        "Three days after Festus arrived in the province, he went up from Cæsarea to Jerusalem.",
        "There the high priest and the leaders of the Jews brought their charges against Paul. They begged Festus",
        "to do them a favor against Paul by sending for him to come to Jerusalem. They were planning to ambush him on the road and kill him.",
        "But Festus answered that Paul was being kept at Cæsarea, and that he himself would be going there soon.",
        "He said, “So let those of you who are in power go down with me and accuse this man there, if he has done anything wrong.”",
        "Festus stayed with them more than ten days and then went down to Cæsarea. The next day he sat on the judgment seat and ordered Paul to be brought in.",
        "When Paul came in, the Jews who had come down from Jerusalem stood around him. They brought many serious charges against Paul, but they could not prove them.",
        "Paul defended himself, saying, “I have done nothing wrong at all, not against the law of the Jews, not against the temple, and not against Cæsar.”",
        "But Festus wanted to do the Jews a favor, so he asked Paul, “Are you willing to go up to Jerusalem and be tried there before me on these charges?”",
        "Paul said, “I am standing before Cæsar’s judgment seat, where I should be tried. I have done nothing wrong to the Jews, as you know very well.”",
        "“If I am guilty, or have done anything that deserves death, I do not refuse to die. But if none of their charges against me are true, no one can hand me over to them. I appeal to Cæsar!”",
        "Then Festus talked it over with his council and answered, “You have appealed to Cæsar? Then to Cæsar you will go!”",
        "A few days later King Agrippa and Bernice came to Cæsarea to pay their respects to Festus.",
        "They stayed there many days, so Festus told the king about Paul’s case. He said, “There is a man here whom Felix left as a prisoner.”",
        "“When I was in Jerusalem, the chief priests and the elders of the Jews brought charges against him and asked me to condemn him.”",
        "“I told them that it is not the Roman way to hand anyone over to die before the accused man has met his accusers face to face and has had a chance to defend himself against the charges.”",
        "“So when they came here, I did not wait. The very next day I sat on the judgment seat and ordered the man to be brought in.”",
        "“When his accusers stood up, they did not charge him with any of the crimes I had expected.”",
        "“Instead, they had some arguments with him about their own superstition, and about a man named Jesus who had died, but whom Paul claimed is alive.”",
        "“I was not sure how to look into questions like these, so I asked him if he would go to Jerusalem and be tried there on these matters.”",
        "“But Paul asked to be held for Augustus (the Emperor) to decide his case. So I ordered him to be kept until I could send him to Cæsar.”",
        "Then Agrippa said to Festus, “I would like to hear this man myself.” Festus said, “Tomorrow you will hear him.”",
