        "In Cæsarea there was a man named Cornelius. He was a centurion (an officer over a hundred soldiers) in the unit called the Italian band.",
        "He was a devout man who feared God, and so did everyone in his household. He gave many gifts to the poor among the people and prayed to God all the time.",
        "One day about three in the afternoon, he clearly saw in a vision an angel of God come to him and say, “Cornelius!”",
        "Cornelius stared at him in fear and said, “What is it, Lord?” The angel told him, “Your prayers and your gifts to the poor have risen up before God, and He remembers them.”",
