        "When we arrived in Rome, the centurion handed the prisoners over to the captain of the guard. But Paul was allowed to live by himself, with a soldier to guard him.",
        "Three days later, Paul called together the leaders of the Jews. When they had gathered, he said to them, “Brothers, I have done nothing against our people or the customs of our fathers. Yet I was handed over as a prisoner from Jerusalem into the hands of the Romans.”",
