        "While Apollos was in Corinth, Paul traveled through the inland region and came to Ephesus. There he found some disciples.",
        "He asked them, “Did you receive the Holy Ghost since you believed?” They answered, “We haven’t even heard that there is a Holy Ghost.”",
        "So he asked them, “Then what were you baptized into?” They said, “Into John’s baptism.”",
        "Paul said, “John baptized with the baptism of repentance. He told the people to believe in the One who would come after him, that is, in Christ Jesus.”",
        "After hearing this, they were baptized in the name of the Lord Jesus.",
        "When Paul laid his hands on them, the Holy Ghost came on them, and they spoke in tongues and prophesied.",
        "There were about twelve men in all.",
        "Paul went into the synagogue and spoke boldly there for three months, reasoning with people and persuading them about the kingdom of God.",
        "But some of them became stubborn and would not believe, and they spoke evil of the Way (the gospel) in front of the crowd. So Paul left them and took the disciples with him, and he reasoned every day in the lecture hall of a man named Tyrannus.",
        "This went on for two years, so that everyone who lived in Asia (the Roman province), both Jews and Greeks, heard the word of the Lord Jesus.",
        "God did unusual miracles through Paul’s hands.",
        "Even handkerchiefs or aprons that had touched his body were taken to the sick, and their diseases left them and the evil spirits went out of them.",
        "Then some Jews who traveled around casting out evil spirits tried to use the name of the Lord Jesus over people who had evil spirits. They said, “We command you by Jesus, whom Paul preaches.”",
        "Seven sons of a Jew named Sceva, a chief priest, were doing this.",
        "But the evil spirit answered them, “I know Jesus, and I know Paul, but who are you?”",
        "Then the man who had the evil spirit jumped on them, overpowered them, and beat them, so that they ran out of that house naked and wounded.",
        "All the Jews and Greeks living in Ephesus heard about this. Fear came over all of them, and the name of the Lord Jesus was greatly honored.",
        "Many who had believed came and confessed, openly telling what they had done.",
        "Many of those who had practiced magic brought their books together and burned them in front of everyone. They added up what the books were worth and found it came to fifty thousand pieces of silver.",
        "In this way the word of the Lord grew powerfully and won out.",
        "After these things were over, Paul decided in the spirit to go to Jerusalem, after passing through Macedonia and Achaia. He said, “After I have been there, I must see Rome too.”",
        "So he sent two of his helpers, Timotheus and Erastus, to Macedonia, but he himself stayed in Asia for a while.",
        "About that time a big disturbance broke out about the Way.",
        "A man named Demetrius, a silversmith who made small silver shrines of Diana, brought in a lot of business for the craftsmen.",
        "He called them together, along with the workers in similar trades, and said, “Men, you know that we earn our wealth from this business.”",
        "“And you see and hear that not only in Ephesus but in almost all of Asia, this Paul has persuaded and turned away a great many people. He says that gods made by human hands are not gods at all.”",
        "“So there is danger not only that our trade will lose its good name, but also that the temple of the great goddess Diana will be treated as nothing, and her greatness will be destroyed, she whom all Asia and the world worship.”",
        "When they heard this, they were filled with rage and shouted, “Great is Diana of the Ephesians!”",
        "The whole city was thrown into confusion. They grabbed Gaius and Aristarchus, men from Macedonia who were traveling with Paul, and all rushed together into the theatre.",
        "Paul wanted to go in to the people, but the disciples wouldn’t let him.",
        "Even some of the leading officials of Asia, who were his friends, sent him a message begging him not to risk going into the theatre.",
        "Some were shouting one thing and some another, because the crowd was confused, and most of them didn’t even know why they had come together.",
        "They pulled Alexander out of the crowd, with the Jews pushing him to the front. Alexander waved his hand for quiet and wanted to make a defense to the people.",
        "But when they realized he was a Jew, they all shouted together for about two hours, “Great is Diana of the Ephesians!”",
        "Finally the town clerk calmed the crowd and said, “Men of Ephesus, who doesn’t know that the city of the Ephesians is the keeper of the temple of the great goddess Diana, and of the image that fell down from Jupiter (from the sky)?”",
        "“Since no one can deny these things, you should calm down and not do anything rash.”",
        "“You have brought these men here, but they haven’t robbed temples or spoken evil against your goddess.”",
        "“So if Demetrius and the craftsmen with him have a complaint against anyone, the courts are open and there are Roman governors. Let them bring charges against each other there.”",
        "“But if you want anything else settled, it will be decided in a lawful assembly.”",
        "“For we are in danger of being charged with rioting because of today’s uproar. There is no reason we could give to explain this mob.”",
        "After he said this, he sent the assembly away."
